,{"affno":"1","first":"Mette M","key":"rosenkildepau","last":"Rosenkilde","locid":"d902feb8-1594-4fa8-bcb1-9f646dc30dd3","name":"Rosenkilde, Mette M.","name_org":"Rosenkilde, Mette M","orcid":"0000-0001-9600-3254","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Jørgen","key":"rungbypau","last":"Rungby","locid":"16f0bbd5-607e-422d-949d-13546554c84e","name":"Rungby, Jørgen","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Majken K","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"adf3a8c7-b701-41a7-944b-36ab93e1b7f4","name":"Jensen, Majken K.","name_org":"Jensen, Majken K","orcid":"0000-0003-4729-7545","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Birgitte","key":"georgpau","last":"Georg","name":"Georg, Birgitte","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Jens","key":"hannibalpau","last":"Hannibal","locid":"b2810b1e-a8c8-41cb-bb4f-669ad1ff6b65","name":"Hannibal, Jens","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Tomasz","key":"brudekpau","last":"Brudek","name":"Brudek, Tomasz","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Susana","key":"aznarpau","last":"Aznar","name":"Aznar, Susana","rank":21,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Nicolai J","key":"weweralbrechtsenpau","last":"Wewer Albrechtsen","locid":"0d59b767-fdca-42a0-b879-70fb0ec55651","name":"Wewer Albrechtsen, Nicolai J","orcid":"0000-0003-4230-5753","rank":22,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40271226"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1210/jendso/bvaf056","issn":["24721972"],"issue":"6","journal":"Journal of the Endocrine Society","paperid":"bvaf056","status":"p","title":"Journal of the Endocrine Society","title_org":"Journal of the endocrine society","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105003642595"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Roskilde University","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-353abb77-8999-4512-8fbe-48229324ddf4","ruc-b8470996-93ca-4699-9ef8-79ed11c9ae0b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"The Glucagon Receptor Is Expressed in the Frontal Cortex and Impaired Signaling Associates With Cognitive Decline","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-804455","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Fat grafting is a gentle technique used to correct soft tissue defects but is challenged by low graft survival rates. To enhance retention, mesenchymal stromal cells (MSCs), have been explored. Autologous MSC-therapy have shown promise but come with logistical and cost challenges. Contrary, allogeneic MSC-therapy offer a more feasible solution, with preclinical studies suggesting improved fat graft retention from allogenic MSC-therapy. This study aimed to expand the preclinical research by investigating the use of cryopreserved allogeneic MSC. METHODS: Using an immunocompetent rat model for autologous fat grafting, the effect of allogeneic MSCs on 3-month fat graft retention was investigated. In a series of experiments the effect of dosing (0.2 x106 - 25 x106 MSC/mL), allogenicity (allogeneic and syngeneic), and cryopreservation was assessed. RESULTS: Our findings did not indicate any beneficial effect from cryopreserved allogeneic MSC-therapy for fat grafting across the tested concentrations. In fact, increasing the dosage resulted in lower fat graft retention, reduced expression of adipose markers and increased fibrosis. Administration of cryopreserved syngeneic MSCs had no beneficial effect on long term fat graft retention either. Substituting cryopreserved MSCs with freshly harvested MSCs also did not enhance fat graft retention. CONCLUSIONS: Unlike previous preclinical studies, our experiments did not reveal a beneficial effect of supplementing fat grafts with MSCs. Given the limited success in translating MSC assisted fat grafting to clinical settings, our study underscores the importance of further investigations to evaluate the efficacy of MSC therapy in enhancing fat graft retention.Clinical Relevance Statement: Our study found no benefit of cryopreserved or freshly cultured allogeneic or syngeneic MSC therapy in improving fat graft retention, challenging the clinical relevance of MSC supplementation for fat grafting and suggesting further research is needed before clinical application. CLINICAL RELEVANCE STATEMENT: Our study found no benefit of cryopreserved or freshly cultured allogeneic or syngeneic MSC therapy in improving fat graft retention, challenging the clinical relevance of MSC supplementation for fat grafting and suggesting further research is needed before clinical application.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Alstrup, Toke","Pedersen, Jonas","Kjær, Emma Mader","Poulsen, Kristine Juul","Steinfurth, Stig","Pedersen, Michael","Møller, Bjarne Kuno","Damsgaard, Tine Engberg","Eijken, Marco"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-806837"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adipose tissue","Animal model","Cellular therapy","Fat grafting","Mesenchymal stromal cell"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mesenchymal stem cell therapy does not enhance fat graft retention cryopreserved and cultured syngeneic and allogeneic mscs in a rat model","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105004021444","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-806837","identifier":[{"id":"40178539","type":"pmid"},{"id":"105004021444","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-7d811b5d-e035-4b8d-9ceb-2e030c1c5147"],"keyword":["Mesenchymal stromal cell","adipose tissue","animal model","cellular therapy","fat grafting","graft retention","soft-tissue reconstruction"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F7CF2A0755B71EDEBA650F8EF42828E1"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Aarhus University Hospital","Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Plastic and Breast surgery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital (AUH)"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["University of Southern Denmark (SDU)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Toke","key":"alstruptokepau","last":"Alstrup","locid":"aa5ce4ef-b371-4a29-87c3-9fc4cfadfc5b","name":"Alstrup, Toke","orcid":"0000-0003-0540-2714","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas Oute","key":"pedersenjonaspau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"a727c815-0f80-4707-a80a-96a6f72b279d","name":"Pedersen, Jonas","name_org":"Pedersen, Jonas Oute","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Emma Mader","key":"kjæremmamaderpau","last":"Kjær","name":"Kjær, Emma Mader","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristine Juul","key":"poulsenkristinejuulpau","last":"Poulsen","name":"Poulsen, Kristine Juul","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Stig","key":"steinfurthstigpau","last":"Steinfurth","name":"Steinfurth, Stig","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"pedersenmichaelpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"849517d4-7243-4520-88f0-7989abe3865a","name":"Pedersen, Michael","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bjarne Kuno","key":"møllerbjarnekunopau","last":"Møller","locid":"1efb651c-6d14-4c30-82e6-998dbb496ae0","name":"Møller, Bjarne Kuno","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Tine Engberg","key":"damsgaardtineengbergpau","last":"Damsgaard","locid":"570d5b9d-393b-4fcb-8e82-874176f3bcaf","name":"Damsgaard, Tine Engberg","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Marco","key":"eijkenmarcopau","last":"Eijken","locid":"fe12c770-d594-4332-96ae-2f1d8d9c0c01","name":"Eijken, Marco","orcid":"0000-0002-9043-3971","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40178539"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1097/prs.0000000000012121","issn":["00321052","15294242"],"issn_org":["00321052"],"journal":"Plastic and Reconstructive Surgery","paperid":"12121","publisher":"Lippincott Williams and Wilkins","status":"e","title":"Plastic and Reconstructive Surgery"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105004021444"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["E-Published (ahead of print)"]},"sid":["au-7d811b5d-e035-4b8d-9ceb-2e030c1c5147"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Mesenchymal stem cell therapy does not enhance fat graft retention : Cryopreserved and cultured syngeneic and allogeneic MSCs in a rat model","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-806837","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVES: To compare pain trajectories and acute exercise-induced pain over a 16-week period in patients with hypermobility spectrum disorder (HSD) undergoing high-load (HEAVY) or low-load (LIGHT) shoulder exercise. METHODS: In this secondary analysis using data from a randomized controlled trial, we included men and women aged 18-65 with HSD and shoulder complaints >3 months. Participants were randomly allocated (1:1 ratio) to 16 weeks of HEAVY or LIGHT shoulder exercise program, performed three times weekly. The HEAVY program consisted of progressive strengthening and full range of motion exercises, while the LIGHT program included low-load exercises performed in neutral to mid-range. Pain was assessed using the numeric rating scale (NRS) before and after each exercise session. Pain trajectories were assessed using pre-exercise pain scores at the final session each week. Exercise-induced pain was evaluated as the change in pain before and after exercise, using the mean of the three sessions each week. Both outcomes were analyzed using linear mixed models. RESULTS: Data from 64 out of 100 patients (HEAVY 34, LIGHT 30) were analyzed (80% women, mean age 39.6, mean Beighton score of 5.8). Shoulder pain was reduced by 0.89 NRS in HEAVY (95% CI 0.4 to 1.4) and 0.33 NRS (95% CI -0.25 to 0.91) in LIGHT. The between-group difference in change in pain from baseline to week 16 was 0.56 (95% CI -0.20 to 1.33, p = 0.149). There was no between-group difference in pain trajectories (group × time interaction, p = 0.321). The mean exercise-induced pain over time was similar in both groups (group × time interaction, p = 0.614), with pain below 0.5 NRS throughout the 16 weeks. CONCLUSIONS: Pain trajectories over 16 weeks were similar in patients with HSD and persistent shoulder complaints performing high-load or low-load shoulder exercises. There was minor to no exercise-induced pain during high-load strengthening exercise, challenging previous beliefs.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Liaghat, Behnam","Juul-Kristensen, Birgit","Christensen, Frederik Holsteen","Nissen, Simon Enghuus","Skou, Søren Thorgaard","Søgaard, Karen","Søndergaard, Jens","Thorlund, Jonas Bloch"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-821218"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Liaghat, Behnam"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Aged","Exercise","Exercise Therapy methods","Female","Humans","Joint Instability therapy","Male","Middle Aged","Pain Measurement","Range of Motion Articular physiology","Shoulder Pain etiology","Young Adult"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pain trajectories and exercise induced pain during 000000000016 weeks of high load or low load shoulder exercise in patients with hypermobile shoulders a secondary analysis of a randomized controlled trial","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1515/sjpain-2024-0072","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was supported by The Ehlers Danlos Society, the Region of Southern Denmark, Esbjerg municipality, The Danish-Rheumatism Association, Fund for Research, Quality and Education in Physiotherapy Practice, and the University of Southern Denmark. Dr. Skou is funded by a program grant from Region Zealand (Exercise First) and by two grants from the European Union’s Horizon 2020 research and innovation program (MOBILIZE, grant agreement No. 801790; and ESCAPE, grant agreement No. 945377)."],"id":"S01-000.00-821218","identifier":[{"id":"40460306","type":"pmid"},{"id":"105008264474","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-4ae69a90-6f78-4d04-8e3d-06287a7ef666"],"ke