iversities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-4ae69a90-6f78-4d04-8e3d-06287a7ef666"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Pain trajectories and exercise-induced pain during 16 weeks of high-load or low-load shoulder exercise in patients with hypermobile shoulders : A secondary analysis of a randomized controlled trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-821218","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"The Ca2+/CaM-dependent protein kinase II alpha (CaMKIIα) is a highly important synaptic protein, which comprises a unique holoenzyme structure organized via the central hub domain. Recently, a distinct binding pocket in the CaMKIIα hub domain was identified for the endogenous neuromodulator γ-hydroxybutyric acid (GHB) and related synthetic analogs. Intriguingly, of the four native CaMKII isozymes, only CaMKIIα accommodates GHB ligands. Key interacting residues in CaMKIIα were revealed, but their involvement in selectivity toward the alpha variant of CaMKII has remained unresolved. Aimed at elucidating the molecular determinants for this selectivity, we here conducted binding studies to CaMKII-HEK whole-cell homogenates using two different in-house–developed GHB-related radioligands, 3-hydroxycyclopent-1-enecarboxylic acid ([3H]HOCPCA) and [3H]O-5-hydroxydiclofenac, in combination with site-directed mutagenesis. Binding to CaMKIIα with the smaller type radioligand [3H]HOCPCA validated key involvement of the four known residues (His395, Arg433, Arg453, and Arg469), but also revealed a role for the upper hub flexible loop containing the CaMKIIα-specific residue Trp403 (Leu in all other CaMKII isozymes) previously suggested to be involved in holoenzyme stability. Insertion of the corresponding residues (L467W/C533R) into CaMKIIβ failed to induce [3H]HOCPCA binding. However, with the larger type radioligand, [3H]O-5-hydroxydiclofenac, specific binding in CaMKIIβ (L467W/C533R) was achieved. Thus, the study confirms involvement of central binding residues and identifies the CaMKIIα flexible pocket loop as a distantly located allosteric factor in determining selectivity of GHB analogs for CaMKIIα. It sheds light on a remarkable interplay of the entire hub cavity for accommodation of ligands and corroborates GHB analogs as CaMKIIα-selective.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Gauger, Stine Juul","Palmelund, Line B.","Tian, Yongsong","Marek, Aleš","Namini, Mathias R.","Griem-Krey, Nane","Petersen, Madeline Y.","Kickinger, Stefanie","Mortensen, Jonas S.","Frølund, Bente","Wellendorph, Petrine"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-819874"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Czechia"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Czech Academy of Sciences"],"keyword":["Homology modelling","Molecular pharmacology","Radioligand binding","Site directed mutagenesis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"allosteric factors in the calcium calmodulin responsive kinase ii hub domain determine selectivity of ghb ligands for camkiiα","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jbc.2025.108543","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-819874","identifier":[{"id":"PMC12148480","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"40286850","type":"pmid"},{"id":"105005486026","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-ab6912d6-146c-4c51-aa7f-ba7a72e999ac"],"keyword":["Ca/calmodulin-dependent protein kinase II (CaMKII)","homology modelling","molecular pharmacology","pocket loop","radioligand binding","site-directed mutagenesis","tryptophan (Trp403)"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-0D8390925C81B8C216EE1EDF5C737B82"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jbc.2025.108543","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/451256163/1-s2.0-S0021925825003928-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Drug Design and Pharmacology, Molecular and Cellular Pharmacology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cz","key":"czech academy of sciences","loc":["Czechia","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Czech Academy of Sciences","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Stine J.","key":"gaugerpau","last":"Gauger","locid":"2f2961ae-ed6c-463f-99b2-2d26f456760e","name":"Gauger, Stine Juul","name_org":"Gauger, Stine J.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Line B.","key":"palmelundpau","last":"Palmelund","locid":"80672c8f-6ae5-4bb4-8b92-4cd3d1958296","name":"Palmelund, Line B.","orcid":"0000-0002-5325-9169","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Yongsong","key":"tianpau","last":"Tian","locid":"d938d8e6-debf-4ecf-8ec2-1f63ea42a9c0","name":"Tian, Yongsong","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Aleš","key":"marekpau","last":"Marek","name":"Marek, Aleš","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mathias R.","key":"naminipau","last":"Namini","name":"Namini, Mathias R.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Nane","key":"griemkreypau","last":"Griem-Krey","locid":"32786a9b-e0ae-4c1c-9c8c-a505940e3232","name":"Griem-Krey, Nane","orcid":"0000-0003-0897-6692","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Madeline Y.","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","name":"Petersen, Madeline Y.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Stefanie","key":"kickingerpau","last":"Kickinger","locid":"dfabeba0-9fe3-4144-83ef-6cdb60401181","name":"Kickinger, Stefanie","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jonas S.","key":"mortensenpau","last":"Mortensen","locid":"08d253fb-ffb3-4eae-b50c-33f6dcad2843","name":"Mortensen, Jonas S.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Bente","key":"frølundpau","last":"Frølund","locid":"b9d5da45-1919-494b-9714-c20a90a98cad","name":"Frølund, Bente","orcid":"0000-0001-5476-6288","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Petrine","key":"wellendorphpau","last":"Wellendorph","locid":"239eb74b-93f3-4ccc-aaca-eecc5bee798f","name":"Wellendorph, Petrine","orcid":"0000-0002-5455-8013","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40286850"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jbc.2025.108543","issn":["00219258","10678816"],"issn_org":["00219258"],"issue":"6","journal":"Journal of Biological Chemistry","paperid":"108543","status":"p","title":"Journal of Biological Chemistry","volume":"301"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105005486026"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-ab6912d6-146c-4c51-aa7f-ba7a72e999ac"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Allosteric factors in the calcium/calmodulin-responsive kinase II hub domain determine selectivity of GHB ligands for CaMKIIα","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-819874","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Normal karyotype acute myeloid leukaemia (NK-AML) in children is a heterogeneous subgroup with scarce data on characteristics and prognosis. We investigated NK-AML in a large paediatric AML cohort from four trials of the Nordic Society for Paediatric Haematology and Oncology-Dutch Belgian Hongkong (NOPHO-DBH) group. Among 1476 AML patients, we identified 316 NK-AML patients (21%). NK-AML was characterized by high frequencies of FLT3 internal tandem duplications (ITD, 33%), mutated NPM1 (28%), WT1 (25%) and CEBPA (21%). Five-year event-free survival (EFS) and overall survival (OS) in NK-AML were 52% (95% confidence interval [CI]: 46-58) and 70% (CI: 65-75) respectively. Restricted to NPM1wt cases only (n = 959), NK-AML was associated with unfavourable outcome (relative risk [RR] of EFS = 0.80, p = 0.014; RR of OS = 0.87, p = 0.022). NK-AML with mutated NPM1 had excellent EFS (79%, CI: 66-88) and OS (97%, CI: 88-99), which was not influenced by concomitant FLT3-ITD. In multivariable analysis, mutated NPM1 in NK-AML was associated with favourable EFS (hazard ratio [HR]: 0.24, CI: 0.13-0.43, p < 0.001) and OS (HR: 0.10, CI: 0.03-0.35, p < 0.001). FLT3-ITD was associated with inferior EFS (HR: 1.56, CI: 1.03-2.35, p = 0.035) and OS (HR: 1.91, CI: 1.11-3.31, p = 0.02). We conclude that prognosis in paediatric NK-AML is independently affected by NPM1 and FLT3-ITD status. Further molecular characterization of NK-AML is needed, especially for NPM1wt NK-AML.","author_count":19,"contributors":["Herlin, Morten Krogh","Kjeldsen, Eigil","Abrahamsson, Jonas","Arad-Cohen, Nira","Cheuk, Daniel","De Moerloose, Barbara","Jahnukainen, Kirsi","Jónsson, Ólafur Gísli","Kaspers, Gertjan J L","Kovalova, Zhanna","Navarro, Jose Maria Fernandez","Noren-Nyström, Ulrika","Palle, Josefine","Pasaulienė, Ramunė","Saks, Kadri","Zeller, Bernward","Holmfeldt, Linda","Hasle, Henrik","Juul-Dam, Kristian Løvvik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-824314"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Asia, Middle East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Belgium","Finland","Hong Kong","Iceland","Israel","Latvia","Lithuania","Netherlands","Norway","Spain","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Amsterdam UMC","Children's Clinical University Hospital","Ghent University Hospital","Helsinki University Central Hospital","Hong Kong Children 's Hospital","Hospital Universitario La Fe","Landspitali University Hospital","Oslo University Hospital","Princess Máxima Center for Pediatric Oncology","Rambam Health Care Campus Israel","Sahlgrenska University Hospital","Umeå University","Uppsala University","Vilnius University Hospital Santaros Klinikos"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"characteristics and prognosis of paediatric normal karyotype acute myeloid leukaemia a nopho dbh aml study","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/bjh.70094","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-824314","identifier":[{"id":"105013668459","type":"scopus"},{"id":"40826900","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-058d302e-a240-4034-8aa0-b7233afd710b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-DC90F4C713BEEE1FE5107C83B6F70834"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/bjh.70094","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University","Aarhus University, Health, Dep