{"abstract":"Background: Acute kidney injury (AKI) and dysnatremia following pediatric cardiac surgery are common conditions associated with worse outcomes. While the multifactorial etiology of AKI is well-known, the role of concomitant dysnatremia is limited. This study aims to describe the occurrence of AKI, its association with the length of stay in the intensive care unit (ICU-LOS), and the impact of dysnatremia in the context of AKI. Methods: Retrospective study comprising 228 congenital heart procedures in 213 infants at Rigshospitalet, Copenhagen, Denmark, from 2017 to 2019. AKI development was evaluated separately in neonates and infants > 1 month and its impact on ICU-LOS. Risk factors for AKI were analyzed across age groups using the univariate and multivariate logistic regression analysis. Results: AKI occurred in 61% of neonates and 62% of infants. Severity was comparable across age groups, except for KDIGO-stage 3, where seven out of eight children treated with peritoneal dialysis were neonates. Urine output was well-preserved despite AKI development, but children with AKI required more than double the furosemide dose. In multivariate analysis, prolonged cardiopulmonary bypass (CPB) duration, higher furosemide doses, and hypernatremia were independently associated with AKI. AKI was only associated with prolonged ICU-LOS in infants, while hyponatremia was associated with prolonged ICU-LOS in all individuals with AKI. Conclusions: AKI occurs frequently in neonates and infants after congenital heart surgery but is only associated with prolonged ICU-LOS in infants. The co-occurrence of AKI and hyponatremia leads to longer ICU-LOS in both neonates and infants. Independent predictors of AKI were prolonged CPB duration, hypernatremia, and reduced furosemide sensitivity.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Kronborg, Jonas Rønne","Lindhardt, Rasmus Bo","Vejlstrup, Niels","Holst, Line Marie","Juul, Klaus","Smerup, Morten Holdgaard","Gjedsted, Jakob","Ravn, Hanne Berg"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-830861"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Kronborg, Jonas Rønne"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"impact of acute kidney injury and dysnatremia on length of stay in infants after cardiac surgery","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00467-025-06846-7","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-830861","identifier":[{"id":"PMC12402015","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"105007942178","type":"scopus"},{"id":"40515779","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-1ddc82ad-f92d-47b4-86e7-89bf6438d391"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-5A32A2ECCB6776F7EA9117E9673AFE35"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/295124200/s00467-025-06846-7.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00467-025-06846-7","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Anaesthesiology and Intensive Care (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas Rønne","key":"kronborgpau","last":"Kronborg","name":"Kronborg, Jonas Rønne","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus Bo","key":"lindhardtpau","last":"Lindhardt","locid":"4f7c12b9-bb3a-4ba4-9fd7-e83aec48dbb7","name":"Lindhardt, Rasmus Bo","orcid":"0000-0002-8649-4640","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels","key":"vejlstruppau","last":"Vejlstrup","name":"Vejlstrup, Niels","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line Marie","key":"holstpau","last":"Holst","name":"Holst, Line Marie","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Klaus","key":"juulpau","last":"Juul","name":"Juul, Klaus","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten Holdgaard","key":"smeruppau","last":"Smerup","name":"Smerup, Morten Holdgaard","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jakob","key":"gjedstedpau","last":"Gjedsted","name":"Gjedsted, Jakob","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanne Berg","key":"ravnpau","last":"Ravn","locid":"25de7650-3dc1-4594-b758-9c36f6de6306","name":"Ravn, Hanne Berg","orcid":"0000-0003-4702-5195","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40515779"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00467-025-06846-7","issn":["0931041X","1432198X"],"issn_org":["0931041X"],"issue":"10","journal":"Pediatric Nephrology","pages":"3281-3291","publisher":"Springer Science+Business Media","status":"e","title":"Pediatric Nephrology","volume":"40"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105007942178"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["E-Published (ahead of print)"]},"sid":["sdu-1ddc82ad-f92d-47b4-86e7-89bf6438d391"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Impact of acute kidney injury and dysnatremia on length of stay in infants after cardiac surgery","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-830861","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Hyperleukocytosis in pediatric acute myeloid leukemia (AML) is associated with severe complications and an inferior outcome. We report results on patients with hyperleukocytosis included in the NOPHO-DBH AML 2012 study. We recommended immediate initiation of full-dose chemotherapy (etoposide monotherapy for 5 days as part of the first course), avoiding leukapheresis and prephase chemotherapy. Of 714 patients included in the NOPHO-DBH AML 2012 study, 122 (17.1%) had hyperleukocytosis, and 111 were treated according to the recommendations with etoposide upfront without preceding leukapheresis or prephase chemotherapy. The first dose was applied the same day as the AML diagnosis or the day after in 94%. Etoposide was administered via peripheral veins in 37% of patients without major complications. After initiation of etoposide the white blood cell counts on days 2-5 were 69%, 36%, 17% and 8%, respectively, of the pre-treatment level. On day 3, 81% of patients had a white blood cell count <100 x109/L. Five-year event-free and overall survival rates for all patients with hyperleukocytosis were 52.9% (95% confidence interval [95% CI]: 44.4-63.0) and 74.1% (95% CI: 66.4-82.6), compared to 64.9% (95% CI: 60.9-69.1) and 78.9% (95% CI: 75.4-82.4) for patients without hyperleukocytosis (P<0.001 for event-free survival, P=0.1 overall survival). Six-week early mortality was 4.1% for all patients with hyperleukocytosis (2.7% for the 111 patients treated with etoposide upfront). We conclude that management of hyperleukocytosis in pediatric AML with immediate etoposide monotherapy without leukapheresis or prephase chemotherapy is feasible, safe and effective. The reduction in white blood cell count during the first days is comparable to the reported results of leukapheresis, and outcomes seem at least equivalent to therapies including leukapheresis. Based on our results, we advocate abandoning leukapheresis for hyperleukocytosis in pediatric AML. Instead, it is crucial to start induction chemotherapy as early as possible.","author_count":20,"contributors":["Zeller, Bernward","Arad-Cohen, Nira","Cheuk, Daniel","De Moerloose, Barbara","Fernandez Navarro, Jose M.","Hasle, Henrik","Jahnukainen, Kirsi","Juul-Dam, Kristian Løvvik","Kaspers, Gertjan","Kovalova, Zanna","Jónsson, Ólafur G.","Lausen, Birgitte","Munthe-Kaas, Monica","Nyström, Ulrika Norén","Palle, Josefine","Pasauliene, Ramune","Pronk, Cornelis J.","Saks, Kadri","Tierens, Anne","Abrahamsson, Jonas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-752690"],"filters":{"added":"2024-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Asia, Middle East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Zeller, Bernward"],"country":["Belgium","Canada","Estonia","Finland","Hong Kong","Iceland","Israel","Latvia","Lithuania","Netherlands","Norway","Spain","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Amsterdam UMC","Children's Clinical University Hospital","Ghent University Hospital","Helsinki University Central Hospital","Hong Kong Children 's Hospital","Hospital Universitario La Fe","Landspitali University Hospital","Oslo University Hospital","Princess Máxima Center for Pediatric Oncology","Rambam Health Care Campus Israel","Skaane University Hospital","Tallinn Children's Hospital","Umeå University","University Health Network","University of Gothenburg","University of Helsinki","Uppsala University","VU University Amsterdam","Vilnius University Hospital Santaros Klinikos"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"management of hyperleukocytosis in pediatric acute myeloid leukemia using immediate chemotherapy without leukapheresis results from the nopho dbh aml 000000002012 protocol","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3324/haematol.2024.285285","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-752690","identifier":[{"id":"38721737","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85203029631","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC11367204","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-26baf8ba-59bf-4be4-8967-8010eb1eaafb"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C37401039B3B3156C72ACF3415235A71"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3324/haematol.2024.285285","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"no","key":"oslo university hospital","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Oslo University Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"il","key":"rambam health care campus israel","loc":["Israel","Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"name":"Rambam Health Care Campus Israel","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"hk","key":"hong kong children s hospital","loc":["Hong Kong","Asia, East"],"name":"Hong Kong Children 's Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"be","key":"ghent university hospital","loc":["Belgium","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Ghent University Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"es","key":"hospital universitario la fe","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Hospital Universitario La Fe","used":1},{"affno":"6","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Paediatrics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"fi","key":"university of helsinki","loc":["Finland","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Helsinki","used":1},{"affno":"8","country":"f