,"name":"Jónsson, Ólafur G.","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"14","corresponding":null,"first":"Birgitte","key":"lausenpau","last":"Lausen","name":"Lausen, Birgitte","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Monica","key":"munthekaaspau","last":"Munthe-Kaas","name":"Munthe-Kaas, Monica","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"15","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulrika Norén","key":"nyströmpau","last":"Nyström","name":"Nyström, Ulrika Norén","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"16","corresponding":null,"first":"Josefine","key":"pallepau","last":"Palle","name":"Palle, Josefine","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"17","corresponding":null,"first":"Ramune","key":"pasaulienepau","last":"Pasauliene","name":"Pasauliene, Ramune","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"18","corresponding":null,"first":"Cornelis J.","key":"pronkpau","last":"Pronk","name":"Pronk, Cornelis J.","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"19","corresponding":null,"first":"Kadri","key":"sakspau","last":"Saks","name":"Saks, Kadri","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"20","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne","key":"tierenspau","last":"Tierens","name":"Tierens, Anne","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"21","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas","key":"abrahamssonpau","last":"Abrahamsson","name":"Abrahamsson, Jonas","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38721737"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3324/haematol.2024.285285","issn":["03906078","15928721"],"issn_org":["03906078"],"issue":"9","journal":"Haematologica","pages":"2873-2883","publisher":"Ferrata Storti Foundation","status":"p","title":"Haematologica","volume":"109"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85203029631"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-26baf8ba-59bf-4be4-8967-8010eb1eaafb"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Management of hyperleukocytosis in pediatric acute myeloid leukemia using immediate chemotherapy without leukapheresis : results from the NOPHO-DBH AML 2012 protocol","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-752690","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Abstract Introduction: Patients with generalised joint hypermobility, including knee hypermobility (GJHk), often experience knee pain and are typically managed with low-intensity strength training and/or proprioceptive training as part of standard care. However, not all patients experience satisfactory outcomes. High-load strength training may offer additional benefits, such as increased muscle cross-sectional area, neural drive and tendon stiffness, which may reduce pain and improve active knee joint stability during movement tasks and daily activities. So far, no randomised controlled trials (RCTs) have compared high-load strength training with traditional treatment strategies (standard care) for this patient group. Methods and analysis: In this RCT, we aim to recruit patients with GJHk and knee pain from primary care physiotherapy clinics in the Region of Southern Denmark and via social media. Patients with competing injuries or experience with high-load strength training will be excluded. Patients will be randomised (1:1 ratio) to either 2 weekly sessions of high-load strength training or standard care for 12 weeks. The primary outcome is self-reported knee pain during an activity nominated by the patient as the most aggravating for their present knee pain measured using the Visual Analogue Scale for Nominated Activity (VASNA, 0-100; 0=no pain and 100=worst imaginable pain). This will be collected at baseline, 6 weeks, 12 weeks and 12 months. Secondary outcomes include self-reported knee function and adverse events (collected at baseline, 12 weeks and 12 months), objective measurements including a 5-repetition maximum single-leg press, proprioception and single-leg-hop for distance (collected at baseline and 12 weeks), and a range of other outcome measures such as fear of movement, tendon stiffness and global perceived effect. We aim to recruit 90 patients in total to detect a 10 mm group difference in the primary outcome with 80% power. Ethics and dissemination: This study was funded by Independent Research Fund Denmark (grant number 2034-00088B) on 14 June 2022; the Regional Committees on Health Research Ethics for Southern Denmark approved it (S-20230050) on 30 August 2023. The first recruitment site opened on 15 February 2024, and the final results will be submitted to a peer-reviewed journal to inform rehabilitation strategies for symptomatic GJHk.Protocol version 1, dated 4 July 2024. Trial registration number: NCT06277401.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Liaghat, Behnam","Bojsen-Møller, Jens","Juul-Kristensen, Birgit","Henriksen, Peter","Mohammadnejad, Afsaneh","Heiberg, Bibi Dige","Thorlund, Jonas Bloch"],"cuid":["S02-098.11-769693"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Liaghat, Behnam"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Arthralgia therapy","Denmark","Female","Humans","Hypermobilitet","Joint Instability therapy","Knee","Knee Joint physiopathology","Male","Musculoskeletal disorders","Pain Management","Physical Therapy Modalities","Randomized Controlled Trial","Randomized Controlled Trials as Topic","Rehabilitation medicine","Resistance Training methods","Styrketræning","Young Adult","disease health science and nursing"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-UCL"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"high load strength training compared with standard care treatment in young adults with joint hypermobility and knee pain study protocol for a randomised controlled trial the hiper knee study","src":["sdu","ucl"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-UCL"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjopen-2024-090812","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-098.11-769693","identifier":[{"id":"39414294","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11487976","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85206602847","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-f54b32ba-24d4-4710-9464-91740e113a44","ucl-a56a6c94-ab07-4d2d-9c10-ddd237320ca3"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Arthralgia/therapy","Denmark","Female","Humans","Hypermobilitet","Joint Instability/therapy","Knee Joint/physiopathology","Knæled","Male","Randomized Controlled Trials as Topic","Resistance Training/methods","Styrketræning","Young Adult","disease, health science and nursing","knee","musculoskeletal disorders","pain management","physical therapy modalities","randomized controlled trial","rehabilitation medicine"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-F57CC2C3DF4E5C593319A355E3B4917B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjopen-2024-090812","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/275697885/e090812.full.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics, Center for Muscle and Joint Health","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics, Research Unit of Musculoskeletal Function and Physiotherapy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ucl university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-UCL","l3nl":"UCL University College","l3nn":"UCL University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"UCL University College","namevar":["UCL Erhvervsakademi og Professionshøjskole, Direktion, Sundhed, Fysioterapeutuddannelsen"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-UCL","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Behnam","key":"liaghatpau","last":"Liaghat","locid":"02a3f8a6-b47d-4c88-9c31-6ffb568e3937","name":"Liaghat, Behnam","orcid":"0000-0002-3050-0028","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens","key":"bojsenmøllerpau","last":"Bojsen-Møller","locid":"0b8727d1-a7f3-4ab6-bcb2-e836c0b320f3","name":"Bojsen-Møller, Jens","orcid":"0000-0001-6737-446X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Birgit","key":"juulkristensenpau","last":"Juul-Kristensen","locid":"887ddfe7-cfa6-4b72-a17d-ecf86987c5c0","name":"Juul-Kristensen, Birgit","orcid":"0000-0002-4973-8415","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"henriksenpau","last":"Henriksen","locid":"694aee1d-b427-4a91-9012-90f8f60500e1","name":"Henriksen, Peter","orcid":"0000-0002-7706-7137","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Afsaneh","key":"mohammadnejadpau","last":"Mohammadnejad","locid":"b84f7891-aa4a-46fb-a0a2-1d377876d9b3","name":"Mohammadnejad, Afsaneh","orcid":"0000-0003-4184-7518","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bibi Dige","key":"heibergpau","last":"Heiberg","locid":"f37b8fd6-1e5f-447a-b2c1-5dfa4b65f310","name":"Heiberg, Bibi Dige","orcid":"0000-0002-0520-0664","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jonas Bloch","key":"thorlundpau","last":"Thorlund","locid":"5b59bfe4-8aff-41d8-8b2d-4b19ab3e56c4","name":"Thorlund, Jonas Bloch","orcid":"0000-0001-7789-8224","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39414294"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1136/bmjopen-2024-090812","issn":["20446055"],"issue":"10","journal":"BMJ Open","paperid":"e090812","publisher":"BMJ Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"BMJ Open","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85206602847"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","UCL University College","Universities","University Colleges","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-f54b32ba-24d4-4710-9464-91740e113a44","ucl-a56a6c94-ab07-4d2d-9c10-ddd237320ca3"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark","UCL University College"],"title":"High-load strength training compared with standard care treatment in young adults with joint hypermobility and knee pain : study protocol for a randomised controlled trial (the HIPEr-Knee study)","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-098.11-769693","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE Measurable residual disease (MRD) by using flow cytometry after induction therapy is strongly prognostic in pediatric AML, and hematopoietic stem-cell transplant (hSCT) may counteract a poor response. We designed a phase III study with intensified response-guided induction and MRD-based risk stratification and treated poor induction response with hSCT. The efficacy of liposomal daunorubicin (DNX) in induction was compared with mitoxantrone. METHODS The study planned to randomly assign 300 patients, but the production of DNX ceased in 2017. One hundred ninety-four patients were randomly assigned to mitoxantrone or experimental DNX in induction 1. Ninety-three non–randomly assigned patients served as an observation cohort. Primary end point was fraction of patients with MRD <0.1% on day 22 after induction 1. Patients with MRD ≥15% after induction 1 or ≥0.1% after induction 2 or FLT3-ITD with NPM1 wildtype were stratified to high-risk therapy, including hSCT. RESULTS Outcome for all 287 children was good with 5-year event-free survival (EFS5y) 66.7% (CI, 61.4 to 72.4) and 5-year overall survival (OS5y) 79.6% (CI, 75.0 to 84.4). Overall, 75% were stratified to standard-risk and 19% to high-risk. There was no difference in the proportion of patients with MRD <0.1% on day 22 after induction 1 (34% mitoxantrone, etoposide, araC [MEC], 30% DNX, P 5 .65), but the proportion increased to 61% for MEC versus 47% for DNX (P 5 .061) at the last evaluation before induction 2. EFS5y was significantly lower, 56.6% (CI, 46.7 to 66.5) versus 71.9% (CI, 63.0 to 80.9), and cumulative incidence of relapse (CIR) was higher, 35.1% (CI, 25.7 to 44.7) versus 18.8% (CI, 11.6 to 27.2) for DNX. The inferior outcome for DNX was only in standard-risk patients with EFS5y 55.3% (CI, 45.1 to 67.7) versus 79.9% (CI, 71.1 to 89.9), CIR 39.5% (CI, 28.4 to 50.3) versus 18.7% (CI, 10.5 to 28.7), and OS5y 76.2% (CI, 67.2 to 86.4) versus 88.6% (CI, 81.4 to 96.3). As-treated analyses, including the observation cohort, supported these results. For all high-risk patients, 85% received hSCT, and EFS5y was 77.7 (CI, 67.3 to 89.7) and OS5y was 83.0 (CI, 73.5 to 93.8). CONCLUSION The intensification of induction therapy with risk stratification on the basis of response to induction and hSCT for high-risk patients led to improved outcomes. Mitoxantrone had a superior anti-leukemic effect than liposomal daunorubicin.","author_count":18,"contributors":["Tierens, Anne","Arad-Cohen, Nira","Cheuk, Daniel","De Moerloose, Barbara","Fernandez Navarro, Jose Maria","Hasle, Henrik","Jahnukainen, Kirsi","Juul-Dam, Kristian Løvvik","Kaspers, Gertjan","Kovalova, Zanna","Lausen, Birgitte","Norén-Nyström, Ulrika","Palle, Josefine","Pasauliene, Ramune","Pronk, Cornelis Jan","Saks, Kadri","Zeller, Bernward","Abrahamsson, Jonas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-745002"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Asia, Middle East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Abrahamsson, Jonas"],"country":["Belgium","Canada","Estonia","Finland","Hong Kong","Israel","Latvia","Lithuania","Netherlands","Norway","Spain","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Amsterdam UMC","Children's Clinical University Hospital","Ghent University Hospital","Helsinki University Central Hospital","Hong Kong Children 's Hospital","Hospital Universitario La Fe","Oslo University Hospital","Princess Máxima Center for Pediatric Oncology","Rambam Health Care Campus Israel","Skaane University Hospital","Tallinn Children's Hospital","Toronto General Hospital","Umeå University","University of Gothenburg","University of Helsinki","Uppsala University","VU University Amsterdam","Vilnius University Hospital Santaros Klinikos"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mitoxantrone versus liposomal daunorubicin in induction of pediatric aml with risk stratification based on flow cytometry measurement of residual disease","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85196212866","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-745002","identifier":[{"id":"38603646","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85196212866","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-a44535fa-8264-4c9c-8f4b-c177372f208f"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FC6BBF429786F2669A61610074267E0B"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ca","key":"toronto general hospital","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Toronto General Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"il","key":"rambam health care campus israel","loc":["Israel","Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"name":"Rambam Health Care Campus Israel","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"hk","key":"hong kong children s hospital","loc":["Hong Kong","Asia, East"],"name":"Hong Kong Children 's Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"be","key":"ghent university hospital","loc":["Belgium","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Ghent University Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"es","key":"hospital universitario la fe","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Hospital Universitario La Fe","used":1},{"affno":"6","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Paediatrics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"fi","key":"university of helsinki","loc":["Finland","Euro