ncidence, clinicopathological risk factors, and outcome in a population-based Danish cohort","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-096.88-767062","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Liposomes carrying chemotherapeutic drugs can accumulate passively in solid tumors at high levels. However, additional targeting of the liposomes towards e.g. receptors expressed on cancer cells may improve their interaction and therapeutic properties. In this study, we designed a liposomal delivery system, which utilizes the intrinsic characteristics of HER2-positive tumors to ensure efficient delivery of oxaliplatin to the cancer cells. On the liposome surface, trastuzumab, an antibody specific to the HER2 receptor, was shown to facilitate internalization by the cancer cells. A polyethylene glycol (PEG) layer on the liposome surface provides protection from mononuclear phagocyte system uptake. To optimize the interaction between liposomes and cancer cells, a protease-sensitive cleavable peptide linker was inserted at the base of each PEG. The PEG layer is then cleaved off by intra- and extracellular matrix metalloproteinases (MMPs) upon accumulation in the tumor. Our data demonstrate that the removal of PEG significantly destabilizes the liposomes and leads to substantial oxaliplatin release. The proposed beneficial effect of combining antibody-mediated internalization with MMP sensitivity was confirmed in a series of in vivo studies using ovarian cancer xenograft models. The results demonstrated that HER2-targeted MMP-sensitive liposomes have superior anticancer activity compared to non-targeted and non-cleavable liposomes.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Juul, Christian Ammitzbøll","Engel, Trine Bjørnbo","Fliedner, Frederikke Petrine","Ringgaard, Lars","Eliasen, Rasmus","Melander, Fredrik","Bak, Martin","Kjaer, Andreas","Henriksen, Jonas Rosager","Elema, Dennis Ringkjøbing","Hansen, Anders Elias","Andresen, Thomas Lars"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-756182"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Andresen, Thomas Lars"],"keyword":["Cancer","HER2","Liposomes","Matrix metalloproteinase","Targeting"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"her000000000002 targeted enzyme activated liposomes show superior in vivo efficacy in an ovarian cancer model","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85194745669","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["We are grateful for the NaSTaR grant given by the European Research Council (ERC) and the Lundbeck Foundation Fellowship. We further thank the Technical University of Denmark for providing additional funding."],"id":"S02-100.00-756182","identifier":[{"id":"85194745669","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38705519","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-aa3f79d3-9c84-433e-96ca-0d04aa34f465","ku-ad00c67c-5728-42d1-bf38-c5c23786e837"],"keyword":["HER2","Liposomes","Matrix metalloproteinase","Targeting","cancer"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-FB49E811768BD974243E89E47AD84823"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","nameva