{"abstract":"Tracing potentially infected contacts of confirmed cases is important when fighting outbreaks of many infectious diseases. The COVID-19 pandemic has motivated researchers to examine how different contact tracing strategies compare in terms of effectiveness (ability to mitigate infections) and cost efficiency (number of prevented infections per isolation). Two important strategies are so-called forward contact tracing (tracing to whom disease spreads) and backward contact tracing (tracing from whom disease spreads). Recently, Kojaku and colleagues reported that backward contact tracing was \"profoundly more effective\" than forward contact tracing, that contact tracing effectiveness \"hinges on reaching the 'source' of infection,\" and that contact tracing outperformed case isolation in terms of cost efficiency. Here we show that these conclusions are not true in general. They were based in part on simulations that vastly overestimated the effectiveness and efficiency of contact tracing. Our results show that the efficiency of contact tracing strategies is highly contextual; faced with a disease outbreak, the disease dynamics determine whether tracing infection sources or new cases is more impactful. Our results also demonstrate the importance of simulating disease spread and mitigation measures in parallel rather than sequentially.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Juul, Jonas L.","Strogatz, Steven H"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-700894"],"filters":{"added":"2023-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Juul, Jonas L."],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Cornell University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"comparing the efficiency of forward and backward contact tracing","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevE.108.034308","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-700894","identifier":[{"id":"37849148","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85172867073","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-647b7a2b-201c-4eb5-82c3-f4182ff56c12"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-88C01D79471410DB11C2AF68226692C7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevE.108.034308","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/338334787/PhysRevE.108.034308.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Cognitive Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"cornell university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Cornell University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas L","key":"juulpau","last":"Juul","locid":"d8293ed2-35e5-4031-8602-349a86b5b33e","name":"Juul, Jonas L.","name_org":"Juul, Jonas L","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Steven H","key":"strogatzpau","last":"Strogatz","name":"Strogatz, Steven H","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37849148"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1103/physreve.108.034308","issn":["24700045","24700053"],"issn_org":["24700045"],"issue":"3","journal":"Physical Review E","paperid":"034308","publisher":"American Physical Society","status":"p","title":"Physical Review E","volume":"108"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85172867073"],"sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-647b7a2b-201c-4eb5-82c3-f4182ff56c12"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Comparing the efficiency of forward and backward contact tracing","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-700894","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Infectious diseases are major health care challenges globally and a prevalent cause of admission to emergency departments. Epidemiologic characteristics and outcomes based on population level data are limited. The Database of Community Acquired Infections in Eastern Denmark (DCAIED) 2018–2021 was established with the aim to explore and estimate the population characteristics, and outcomes of patients suffering from community acquired infections at the emergency departments in the Capital Region and the Zealand Region of Denmark using data from electronic medical records. Adult patients (≥18 years) presenting to the emergency department with suspected or confirmed infection are included in the cohort. Presence of sepsis and organ failure are assessed using modified criteria from the Third International Consensus Definitions for Sepsis and Septic Shock (Sepsis-3). During the inclusion period from January 2018 to January 2022, 2,241,652 adult emergency department visits have been registered. Of these, 451,825 were unique encounters of which 60,316 fulfilled criteria of suspected infection and 28,472 fulfilled sepsis criteria and 8,027 were defined as septic shock. The database covers the entire Capital and Zealand Region of Denmark with an uptake area of 2.6 million inhabitants and includes demographic, laboratory and outcome indicators, with complete follow-up. The database is well-suited for epidemiological research for future national and international collaborations.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Holler, Jon Gitz","Jensen, Jens Ulrik Stæhr","Engsig, Frederik Neess","Bestle, Morten H.","Lindegaard, Birgitte","Rasmussen, Jens Henning","Bundgaard, Henning","Nielsen, Finn Erland","Iversen, Kasper","Larsen, Jesper Juul","Holzknecht, Barbara Juliane","Boel, Jonas","Sivapalan, Pradeesh","Itenov, Theis Skovsgaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-732349"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Community acquired","Database","Emergency department","Epidemiology","Infectious diseases","Sepsis","Shock"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"existing data sources in clinical epidemiology database of community acquired infections requiring hospital referral in eastern denmark dcaied 000000002018 000000002021","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2147/CLEP.S413403","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-732349","identifier":[{"id":"37700929","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85171350357","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10493095","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-c557941a-68a5-48c1-9a38-9e4f43e130b0"],"keyword":["community acquired","database","emergency department","epidemiology","infectious diseases","sepsis","shock"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D693AA78F1203F97C1006DB9ED50AD66"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/386377781/CLEP_413403_existing_data_sources_in_clinical_epidemiology_database_of_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2147/CLEP.S413403","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital – North Zealand"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l