{"abstract":"In the last decade, lithium-ion batteries (LIBs) have become ubiquitous in many technological fields. However, their diagnostics and remaining lifetime estimation are far from being established. To this end, an important aspect is establishing a correlation between the physical changes occurring to the battery materials upon aging and the data obtained by non-destructive measurements. In this paper, we report a methodology for post-mortem analysis of LiFePO4/Graphite batteries involving a range of experimental techniques, including scanning electron microscopy, Raman spectroscopy, and electrochemical impedance spectroscopy, as well as some preliminary results on the correlation of observed microscopic changes and aging parameters. In particular, a larger cycle depth and higher average state-of-charge led to increased battery degradation manifested as morphological and composition changes in anode and cathode, respectively.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Li, Yaqi","Søgaard, Alex Juul","Sørensen, Jonas Ilum","Guo, Jia","Stroe, Daniel-Ioan","Pedersen, Kjeld","Gurevich, Leonid"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-114566"],"event":{"end":"2022-10-13","place":"Detroit, us","start":"2022-10-09","title":"2022 IEEE Energy Conversion Congress and Exposition (ECCE)","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2022-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Lithium ion battery","Post mortem analysis","State of health"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"aging mechanisms of electrodes in lifepo000000000004 graphite batteries","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85144020893&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-114566","identifier":[{"id":"85144020893","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-ddda0ade-911a-4d53-9e05-b68d5920e88a"],"keyword":["Lithium-ion Battery","Post-mortem Analysis","State of Health"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BAAE9450CF3CE76F96571183EA4B8F76"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Hydrogen and Electro-fuels","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Materials and Production","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Materials and Production, Physics","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Materials and Production, Physics and Mechanics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Yaqi","key":"lipau","last":"Li","locid":"780a90f9-d321-4cc6-a22b-818a6b21c979","name":"Li, Yaqi","orcid":"0000-0003-3815-1245","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alex Juul","key":"søgaardpau","last":"Søgaard","locid":"95d344f3-9823-42fa-83a5-02dfd8ff6fd9","name":"Søgaard, Alex Juul","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jonas Ilum","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"0b9408ec-d2ea-44bb-869a-6f06ee3f891a","name":"Sørensen, Jonas Ilum","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jia","key":"guopau","last":"Guo","locid":"1498725c-1800-45d8-8394-11d9dc0b8324","name":"Guo, Jia","orcid":"0000-0002-3882-9266","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Daniel-Ioan","key":"stroepau","last":"Stroe","locid":"5811b49e-3576-45ee-847b-ca093b034b5d","name":"Stroe, Daniel-Ioan","orcid":"0000-0002-2938-8921","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kjeld","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"ff5fc0ab-1fa1-47a2-916c-8b7556f2f938","name":"Pedersen, Kjeld","orcid":"0000-0002-6835-1566","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Leonid","key":"gurevichpau","last":"Gurevich","locid":"2f0f1868-72f6-4a75-ac4d-cd4ad4c82f0c","name":"Gurevich, Leonid","orcid":"0000-0002-5777-2541","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/ecce50734.2022.9947680","eisbn":["9781728193878"],"isbn":["9781728193885"],"issn":["23293721"],"publisher":"IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers)","series":"IEEE Energy Conversion Congress and Exposition","status":"p","title":"2022 IEEE Energy Conversion Congress and Exposition"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85144020893"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-ddda0ade-911a-4d53-9e05-b68d5920e88a"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Aging Mechanisms of Electrodes in LiFePO4/Graphite Batteries","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-114566","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Patients with ischaemic stroke due to large vessel occlusion (LVO) are treated with thrombolysis before thrombectomy, if eligible, as recommended in current guidelines. However, new randomised controlled trials (RCTs) suggest, that pretreatment with thrombolysis may not be necessary in patients with LVO presenting directly at a thrombectomy-capable centre. In this review, we both gather the current knowledge on the treatment of ischaemic stroke due to LVO and evaluate on, whether this should be revised in the view of new RCTs.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Jensen, Luna Juul","Jensen, Jonas","Simonsen, Claus Ziegler"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-164893"],"filters":{"added":"2022-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Jensen, Luna Juul"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"trombolyse forud for trombektomi i behandlingen af patienter med iskæmisk apopleksi","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/331131526/Trombolyse_forud_for_trombektomi_i_behandlingen_af_patienter_med_isk_misk_apopleksi.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-164893","identifier":[{"id":"34596525","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85129863843","type":"scopus"},{"id":"85118096749","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-3e729015-33e3-4583-917f-83ce47cae9a5"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-ADD699B96BCF17CB5BC1FED395738E11"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/331131526/Trombolyse_forud_for_trombektomi_i_behandlingen_af_patienter_med_isk_misk_apopleksi.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Radiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Luna Juul","key":"jensenlunajuulpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Luna Juul","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jonas","key":"jensenjonaspau","last":"Jensen","locid":"f06ea17b-2e51-4d7c-b6c1-eff65fc08484","name":"Jensen, Jonas","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Claus Ziegler","key":"simonsenclauszieglerpau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"ccf2fb52-6a4a-45b2-adb0-d6e83324879f","name":"Simonsen, Claus Ziegler","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34596525"],"pub":{"issn":["00415782","13994174"],"issn_org":["00415782"],"issue":"37","journal":"Ugeskrift for Læger","paperid":"V04210331","publisher":"Almindelige Danske Lægeforening","status":"p","title":"Ugeskrift for Læger","volume":"183"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85129863843"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-3e729015-33e3-4583-917f-83ce47cae9a5"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Trombolyse forud for trombektomi i behandlingen af patienter med iskæmisk apopleksi","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-164893","year":"2022","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Background: Dysnatremia after surgery for congenital heart disease (CHD) is well known and has been associated with prolonged pediatric intensive care unit length of stay (PICU-LOS). Fluctuations in plasma sodium levels occur perioperatively. The primary aim of the study was to evaluate the occurrence of dysnatremia during the first 48 h after surgery and whether it was associated with PICU-LOS. The secondary aim was to evaluate if the degree of sodium fluctuations was associated with PICU-LOS. Methods: A retrospective observational, single-center study including infants undergoing surgery for CHD. The highest and lowest plasma sodium value was registered for the prespecified time periods. PICU-LOS was analyzed in relation to the occurrence of dysnatremia and the degree of plasma sodium fluctuations. The occurrence of dysnatremia was evaluated in relation to surgical procedure and fluid administration. Results: Two hundred and thirty infants who underwent 249 surgical procedures were included. Dysnatremia developed in more than 60% within 48 h after surgery. Infants with normonatremia had a 40%–50% shorter PICU-LOS among children in RACHS-1 category 3–6, compared with infants developing either hypo- or hyper-/hyponatremia within 48 h after surgery (p =.006). Infants who had a decline of plasma sodium >11 mmol/L had almost double the PICU-LOS compared to those with a decline of <8 mmol/L. Conclusion: Dysnatremias were common after surgery for CHD and associated with prolonged PICU-LOS. The degree of decline in plasma sodium was significantly associated with PICU-LOS. Fluid administration both in terms of volume and components (blood products and crystalloids) as well as diuresis were related to the occurrence of dysnatremias.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Kronborg, Jonas Rønne","Lindhardt, Rasmus Bo","Vejlstrup, Niels","Holst, Line Marie","Juul, Klaus","Smerup, Morten","Gjedsted, Jakob","Ravn, Hanne Berg"],"cuid":["S02-088.24-041246"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Kronborg, Jonas Rønne"],"keyword":["Cardiopulmonary Bypass","Congenital heart disease","Heart surgery","Hypernatremia","Hyponatremia","Infant","Intensive care","Length of Stay","Water Electrolyte Imbalance"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"postoperative dysnatremia in infants after open heart surgery occurs frequently and is associated with prolonged intensive care length of stay","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/196826647/aas.14009.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Support was provided from Departmental sources and by a grant from Rigshospitalet, Copenhagen University Hospital, Denmark."],"id":"S02-088.24-041246","identifier":[{"id":"34870843","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85121327522","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-2f8a534f-eb36-449d-b8f8-8b47632f84e3","sdu-dc53917e-2db4-4782-9052-184c38b3be81"],"keyword":["cardiopulmonary bypass","congenital heart disease","heart surgery","hypernatremia","hyponatremia","infant","intensive care","length of stay","water-electrolyte imbalance"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-A54B16DF4BB18EE222088BECC36F9038"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/196826647/aas.14009.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/305421441/LINI_aas.14009.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Cardiothoracic Surgery","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Anaesthesiology and Intensive Care (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jonas Rønne","key":"kronborgpau","last":"Kronborg","name":"Kronborg, Jonas Rønne","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Rasmus Bo","key":"lindhardtpau","last":"Lindhardt","name":"Lindhardt, Rasmus Bo","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Niels","key":"vejlstruppau","last":"Vejlstrup","name":"Vejlstrup, Niels","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Line Marie","key":"holstpau","last":"Holst","name":"Holst, Line Marie","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Klaus","key":"juulpau","last":"Juul","name":"Juul, Klaus","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Morten Holdgaard","key":"smeruppau","last":"Smerup","locid":"633e94fc-6b5d-4f20-a683-bdd98c96ccdc","name":"Smerup, Morten","name_org":"Smerup, Morten Holdgaard","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jakob","key":"gjedstedpau","last":"Gjedsted","locid":"54fce86d-8197-4174-837f-e292be0306e7","name":"Gjedsted, Jakob","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1 3","first":"Hanne Berg","key":"ravnpau","last":"Ravn","locid":"3049e7b7-0f18-413b-88ab-a3d77ebc079b","name":"Ravn, Hanne Berg","orcid":"0000-0003-4702-5195","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34870843"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/aas.14009","issn":["00015172"],"issue":"3","journal":"Acta Anaesthesiologica Scandinavica","pages":"337-344","publisher":"Wiley","status":"p","title":"Acta Anaesthesiologica Scandinavica","volume":"66"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85121327522"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-2f8a534f-eb36-449d-b8f8-8b47632f84e3","sdu-dc53917e-2db4-4782-9052-184c38b3be81"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Postoperative dysnatremia in infants after open-heart surgery occurs frequently and is associated with prolonged intensive care length of stay","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-088.24-041246","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Objectives: Antibodies to severe acute respiratory syndrome coronavirus-2 (SARS-CoV-2) are a key factor in protecting against coronavirus disease 2019 (COVID-19). We examined longitudinal changes in seroprevalence in healthcare workers (HCWs) in Copenhagen and the protective effect of antibodies against SARS-CoV-2. Methods: In this prospective study, screening for antibodies against SARS-CoV-2 (ELISA) was offered to HCWs three times over 6 months. HCW characteristics were obtained by questionnaires. The study was registered at ClinicalTrials.gov, NCT04346186. Results: From April to October 2020 we screened 44 698 HCWs, of whom 2811 were seropositive at least once. The seroprevalence increased from 4.0% (1501/37 452) to 7.4% (2022/27 457) during the period (p < 0.001) and was significantly higher than in non-HCWs. Frontline HCWs had a significantly increased risk of seropositivity compared to non-frontline HCWs, with risk ratios (RRs) at the three rounds of 1.49 (95%CI 1.34–1.65, p < 0.001), 1.52 (1.39–1.68, p < 0.001) and 1.50 (1.38–1.64, p < 0.001). The seroprevalence was 1.42- to 2.25-fold higher (p < 0.001) in HCWs from dedicated COVID-19 wards than in other frontline HCWs. Seropositive HCWs had an RR of 0.35 (0.15–0.85, p 0.012) of reinfection during the following 6 months, and 2115 out of 2248 (95%) of those who were seropositive during rounds one or two remained seropositive after 4–6 months. The 133 of 2248 participants (5.0%) who seroreverted were slightly older and reported fewer symptoms than other seropositive participants. Conclusions: HCWs remained at increased risk of infection with SARS-CoV-2 during the 6-month period. Seropositivity against SARS-CoV-2 persisted for at least 6 months in the vast majority of HCWs and was associated with a significantly lower risk of reinfection.","author_count":31,"contributors":["Iversen, Kasper","Kristensen, Jonas Henrik","Hasselbalch, Rasmus Bo","Pries-Heje, Mia","Nielsen, Pernille Brok","Knudsen, Andreas Dehlbæk","Fogh, Kamille","Norsk, Jakob Boesgaard","Andersen, Ove","Fischer, Thea Køhler","Juul Jensen, Claus Antonio","Torp-Pedersen, Christian","Rungby, Jørgen","Ditlev, Sisse Bolm","Hageman, Ida","Møgelvang, Rasmus","Gybel-Brask, Mikkel","Dessau, Ram B.","Sørensen, Erik","Harritshøj, Lene","Folke, Fredrik","Sten, Curt","Engel Møller, Maria Elizabeth","Benfield, Thomas","Ullum, Henrik","Jørgensen, Charlotte Sværke","Erikstrup, Christian","Ostrowski, Sisse R.","Nielsen, Susanne Dam","Bundgaard, Henning"],"cuid":["S03-100.00-024022"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Iversen, Kasper"],"keyword":["Antibodies Viral","COVID","COVID 19 epidemiology","Cohort Studies","Denmark epidemiology","Health Personnel","Healthcare workers","Humans","Immune response","Prospective Studies","Reinfection","SARS CoV 2","Seroepidemiologic Studies","Seroprevalence"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"seroprevalence of sars cov 000000000002 antibodies and reduced risk of reinfection through 000000000006 months a danish observational cohort study of 000000000044 000000000000 healthcare workers","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC8447554/pdf/main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-100.00-024022","identifier":[{"id":"34543759","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC8447554","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85116788811","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-9bd0933e-b051-48f8-bb53-fbcff4260867","ku