31-834d-fd06962e0567","name":"Pedersen, Julie Rønne","orcid":"0000-0002-7924-5312","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"James","key":"youngpau","last":"Young","locid":"358a4251-6873-4b1b-99df-826eaf19035d","name":"Young, James J.","name_org":"Young, James","orcid":"0000-0003-1210-3106","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jonas Bloch","key":"thorlundpau","last":"Thorlund","locid":"5b59bfe4-8aff-41d8-8b2d-4b19ab3e56c4","name":"Thorlund, Jonas Bloch","orcid":"0000-0001-7789-8224","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Birgit","key":"juulkristensenpau","last":"Juul-Kristensen","locid":"887ddfe7-cfa6-4b72-a17d-ecf86987c5c0","name":"Juul-Kristensen, Birgit","orcid":"0000-0002-4973-8415","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten Bogh","key":"juhlpau","last":"Juhl","locid":"9381fad1-5721-4b98-ac99-7df1c6e4d837","name":"Juhl, Carsten Bogh","orcid":"0000-0001-8456-5364","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-b8bc7afa-b746-4379-9ca7-5e353a542280"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Joint hypermobility in athletes is associated with shoulder injury and shoulder pain: a systematic review and meta-analysis","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-626185","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Aim: To assess the effects of dapagliflozin, metformin and exercise treatment on changes in plasma glucagon concentrations in individuals with overweight and HbA1c-defined prediabetes. Materials and Methods: One-hundred and twenty individuals with overweight (body mass index >= 25 kg/m(2)) and prediabetes (HbA1c of 39-47 mmol/mol) were randomized to a 13-week intervention with dapagliflozin (10 mg once daily), metformin (850 mg twice daily), exercise (30 minutes of interval training 5 days per week) or control (habitual living). A 75-g oral glucose tolerance test (OGTT) (0, 30, 60 and 120 minutes) was administered at baseline, at 13 weeks (end of intervention) and at 26 weeks (end of follow-up). Linear mixed effects models with participant-specific random intercepts were used to investigate associations of the interventions with fasting plasma glucagon concentration, insulin/glucagon ratio and glucagon suppression during the OGTT. Results: At baseline, the median (Q1; Q3) age was 62 (54; 68) years, median fasting plasma glucagon concentration was 11 (7; 15) pmol/L, mean (SD) HbA1c was 40.9 (2.3) mmol/mol and 56% were women. Compared with the control group, fasting glucagon did not change in any of the groups from baseline to the end of the intervention (dapagliflozin group: -5% [95% CI: -29; 26]; exercise group: -8% [95% CI: -31; 24]; metformin group: -2% [95% CI: -27; 30]). Likewise, there were no differences in insulin/glucagon ratio and glucagon suppression during the OGTT between the groups. Conclusions: In individuals with prediabetes, 13 weeks of treatment with dapagliflozin, metformin or exercise was not associated with changes in fasting or post-OGTT glucagon concentrations.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Clemmensen, Kim K. B.","Blond, Martin B.","Amadid, Hanan","Bruhn, Lea","Vistisen, Dorte","Karstoft, Kristian","Persson, Frederik","Ried-Larsen, Mathias","Holst, Jens Juul","Wewer Albrechtsen, Nicolai J","Torekov, Signe Sørensen","Quist, Jonas S.","Jorgensen, Marit E.","Færch, Kristine"],"cuid":["S02-097.30-040022"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Clemmensen, Kim K.B."],"keyword":["Beta cell function","Exercise","GLP 1","Glucagon","Glucose","Insulin Resistance","Metformin","Obesity","Prediabetes","Responses","Sodium glucose co transporter 2 inhibitor","Weight loss"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-STENO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-STENO","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"no effects of dapagliflozin metformin or exercise on plasma glucagon concentrations in individuals with prediabetes a post hoc analysis from the randomized controlled pre d trial","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/182492241/dom.14246.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["We are grateful to the study participants for their cooperation and willingness to participate. The laboratory technicians Hanne Vishof, Lars Sander Koch, Sara Sidenius and Camilla Søs Nielsen at SDCC are thanked for their great dedication, skilled assistance and coordination. Christian S. Hansen, Narges Safai, Nicklas J. Johansen and Johan I. B. Egholk at SDCC, are thanked for their assistance during the study. The authors thank Lene Albæk for outstanding technical assistance with the glucagon measurements. This work was supported by the Novo Nordisk Foundation, AstraZeneca AB, the Danish Innovation Foundation, and University of Copenhagen. K.F., D.V., J.S.Q., H.A., L.B., F.P., K.K.B.C., M.B.B. and M.E.J. are employed by Steno Diabetes Center Copenhagen, a research hospital working in the Danish National Health Service. Until 31 December 2016, Steno Diabetes Center was owned by Novo Nordisk A/S and received part of its core funding from unrestricted grants from the Novo Nordisk Foundation and Novo Nordisk A/S. K.F., H.A., D.V. and M.E.J. own shares in Novo Nordisk A/S. K.F. has received research support from AstraZeneca and Unilever. M.R.‐L. has received personal lecture fees from Novo Nordisk A/S. F.P. has received research grants from AstraZeneca, Novo Nordisk, Novartis and lecture fees from MSD, AstraZeneca, Novo Nordisk, Novartis, Eli Lilly and Boehringer Ingelheim and has served as a consultant for AstraZeneca, Novo Nordisk, Amgen and MSD. M.E.J. has received research grants from Amgen, Sanofi Aventis, Boehringer Ingelheim and AstraZeneca. K.K., J.J.H., N.J.W.A. and S.S.T. have nothing to declare."],"id":"S02-097.30-040022","identifier":[{"id":"33146457","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85096652496","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000590128700001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["ku-0aababd1-737b-4ef2-a8b1-81abcdc71243","sdu-648fe11d-60d2-4e19-9f12-e0fcff4b90c7"],"keyword":["BETA-CELL FUNCTION","COTRANSPORTER 2 INHIBITION","GLP-1","GLUCOSE","INSULIN-RESISTANCE","RESPONSES","WEIGHT-LOSS","exercise","exercise, glucagon, metformin, obesity, prediabetes, sodium-glucose co-transporter-2 inhibitor","glucagon","metformin","obesity","prediabetes","sodium-glucose co-transporter-2 inhibitor"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-602D29205993DAD31493E2092217EC2E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/317366305/dom.14246_2_29.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/182492241/dom.14246.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"steno diabetes centers","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-STENO","l3nn":"Steno Diab