Henrik","key":"ullumhenrikpau","last":"Ullum","locid":"ef594d49-5aeb-4d32-80b4-4bfc281b5cbb","name":"Ullum, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-7306-9058","rank":28,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32758438"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/s1473-3099(20)30589-2","issn":["14733099","14744457"],"issn_org":["14733099"],"issue":"12","journal":"The Lancet Infectious Diseases","pages":"1401-1408","status":"p","title":"The Lancet Infectious Diseases","volume":"20"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85089980210"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-c234fef5-ea5b-4743-8fcf-bd1715a35d6b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Risk of COVID-19 in health-care workers in Denmark : an observational cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-509369","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Fasting duration has been associated with lower fasting blood glucose levels, but higher 2-h post-load levels, and research has indicated an adverse effect of ‘weekend behavior’ on human metabolism. We investigated associations of fasting duration and weekday of examination with glucose, insulin, glucagon and incretin responses to an oral glucose tolerance test (OGTT). This cross-sectional study is based on data from the ADDITION-PRO study, where 2082 individuals attended a health examination including an OGTT. Linear regression analysis was applied to study the associations of overnight fasting duration and day of the week with glucose, insulin, glucagon, glucose-dependent insulinotropic polypeptide (GIP) and glucagon-like peptide 1 (GLP-1) responses to an OGTT. We found that a 1 h longer fasting duration was associated with 1.7% (95% CI: 0.8,2.5) higher 2-h glucose levels, as well as a 3.0% (95% CI: 1.3,4.7) higher GIP and 2.3% (95% CI: 0.3,4.4) higher GLP-1 response. Fasting insulin levels were 20.6% (95% CI: 11.2,30.7) higher on Mondays compared to the other weekdays, with similar fasting glucose levels (1.7%, 95% CI: 0.0,3.4). In this study, longer overnight fasting duration was associated with a worsening of glucose tolerance and increased incretin response to oral glucose. We found higher fasting insulin levels on Mondays compared to the other days of the week, potentially indicating a worsened glucose regulation after the weekend.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Clemmensen, Kim K.B.","Quist, Jonas S.","Vistisen, Dorte","Witte, Daniel R","Jonsson, Anna","Pedersen, Oluf","Hansen, Torben","Holst, Jens J.","Lauritzen, Torsten","Jørgensen, Marit E.","Torekov, Signe","Færch, Kristine"],"cuid":["S03-100.00-027659"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Clemmensen, Kim K.B."],"keyword":["Fasting duration","Incretin","Metabolism","Oral glucose tolerance test","Weekday"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-STENO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-STENO","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"role of fasting duration and weekday in incretin and glucose regulation","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1530/EC-20-0009","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["K K B C, J S Q, D V, M E J and K F are employed by Steno Diabetes Center Copenhagen, a research hospital working in the Danish National Health Service. Until 31 December 2016 Steno Diabetes Center was owned by Novo Nordisk A/S and received part of its core funding from unrestricted grants from the Novo Nordisk Foundation and Novo Nordisk A/S. K K B C, K F, D V and M E J own shares in Novo Nordisk A/S. The other authors have nothing to disclose. The ADDITION-Denmark study was funded by the National Health Services in the counties of Copenhagen, Aarhus, Ringkøbing, Ribe, and Southern Jutland in Denmark; the Danish Council for Strategic Research; the Danish Research ?oundation for ?eneral ?ractice; Novo Nordisk ?oundation; the Danish Centre for Evaluation and Health ?echnology Assessment; the Diabetes ?und of the National Board of Health; the Danish Medical Research Council and the Aarhus University Research Foundation. The ADDITION-PRO study was funded by an unrestricted grant from the European ?oundation for the Study of Diabetes/?fizer for Research into cardiovascular disease risk reduction in patients with diabetes (74550801), the Danish Council for Strategic Research and internal research and equipment funds from Steno Diabetes Center. Between 2000 and 2011, the ADDITION study (screening and intensive treatment of type 2 diabetes in primary care) received unrestricted grants from the medical industry: Novo Nordisk AS, Novo Nordisk Scandinavia AB, AS?RA Denmark, ?fizer Denmark, GlaxoSmithKline Pharma Denmark, SERVIER Denmark A/S and HemoCue Denmark A/S."],"id":"S03-100.00-027659","identifier":[{"id":"32163918","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC7159259","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85083226983","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-ce85f6d8-6f14-46b6-bdd2-7a638d89fadf","ku-619778de-2d68-41a0-9478-6fbc4501c0db","sdu-4956e721-c0bf-4cc7-85ad-561242a8af1d"],"keyword":["Fasting duration","Incretin","Metabolism","Oral glucose tolerance test","Weekday"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-ABA757E27696406C293ED0CACDB0E71B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1530/EC-20-0009","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/244653897/OA_Role_of_fasting_duration_and_weekday_in_incretin.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/169276189/_20493614_Endocrine_Connections_Role_of_fasting_duration_and_weekday_in_incretin_and_glucose_regulation.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"steno diabetes centers","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-STENO","l3nn":"Steno Diabetes Centers","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Steno Diabetes Centers","namevar":["Steno Diabetes Centre Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-STENO","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus Un