id":"101080","publisher":"Elsevier BV","status":"p","title":"Molecular Metabolism","volume":"42"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85092154036"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-08d117a8-ff73-49ca-8896-55dfc74dfa4a","ku-a3aa669a-5ae6-452c-899c-8bd9411cbea4"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Glucagon acutely regulates hepatic amino acid catabolism and the effect may be disturbed by steatosis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.89-013232","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Contagion, broadly construed, refers to anything that can spread infectiously from peer to peer. Examples include communicable diseases, rumors, misinformation, ideas, innovations, bank failures, and electrical blackouts. Sometimes, as in the 1918 Spanish flu epidemic, a contagion mutates at some point as it spreads through a network. Here, using a simple susceptible-infected model of contagion, we explore the downstream impact of a single mutation event. Assuming that this mutation occurs at a random node in the contact network, we calculate the distribution of the number of \"descendants,\" d, downstream from the initial \"patient zero\" mutant. We find that the tail of the distribution decays as d(-2) for complete graphs, random graphs, small-world networks, networks with block-like structure, and other infinite-dimensional networks. This prediction agrees with the observed statistics of memes propagating and mutating on Facebook and is expected to hold for other effectively infinite-dimensional networks, such as the global human contact network. In a wider context, our approach suggests a possible starting point for a mesoscopic theory of contagion. Such a theory would focus on the paths traced by a spreading contagion, thereby furnishing an intermediate level of description between that of individual nodes and the total infected population. We anticipate that contagion pathways will hold valuable lessons, given their role as the conduits through which single mutations, innovations, or failures can sweep through a network as a whole.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Juul, Jonas S.","Strogatz, Steven H."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-520285"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Cornell University"],"keyword":["Dimension","Evolution","Graphs","Physics","SPREAD"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"descendant distributions for the impact of mutant contagion on networks","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevResearch.2.033005","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-520285","identifier":[{"id":"000604136900008","type":"wos"},{"id":"85094820876","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-d4588697-88ec-418b-ac5c-bab483331d53"],"keyword":["CASCADES","DIMENSION","EVOLUTION","GRAPHS","PHYSICS","SPREAD"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CF12E83D251EDCCCED274A98562BECC0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevResearch.2.033005","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/255449521/PhysRevResearch.2.033005.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Niels Bohr Institute, Biocomplexity"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"cornell university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Cornell University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jonas S.","key":"juulpau","last":"Juul","locid":"4298e83e-ac49-4e04-9ea8-f26559478f2b","name":"Juul, Jonas S.","orcid":"0000-0002-5728-9269","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Steven H.","key":"strogatzpau","last":"Strogatz","name":"Strogatz, Steven H.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1103/physrevresearch.2.033005","issn":["26431564"],"issue":"3","journal":"Physical Review Research","paperid":"033005","status":"p","title":"Physical Review Research","volume":"2"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85094820876"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-d4588697-88ec-418b-ac5c-bab483331d53"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Descendant distributions for the impact of mutant contagion on networks","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-520285","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Children with complex CHD are at risk for psychopathology such as severe attention-deficit/hyperactivity disorder symptoms after congenital heart surgery. OBJECTIVE: The aim of this study was to investigate if children with Ventricular Septal Defect, Transposition of Great Arteries, or Tetralogy of Fallot have an increased occurrence of attention-deficit/hyperactivity disorder symptoms compared with the background population and to investigate differences between the three CHDs in terms of occurrence and appearance of attention-deficit/hyperactivity disorder symptoms. METHOD: A national register-based survey was conducted, including children aged 10-16 years with surgically corrected CHDs without genetic abnormalities and syndromes. The Attention-Deficit/Hyperactivity Disorder-Rating Scale questionnaires were filled in by parents and school teachers. RESULTS: In total, 159 out of 283 questionnaires were completed among children with CHDs and compared with age- and sex-matched controls. Children with CHDs had significantly increased inattention scores (p = 0.009) and total attention-deficit/hyperactivity disorder scores (p = 0.008) compared with controls. Post hoc analyses revealed that children with Tetralogy of Fallot had significantly higher inattention scores compared with children both with Ventricular Septal Defect (p = 0.043) and controls (p = 0.004). CONCLUSION: Attention-deficit/hyperactivity disorder symptoms and inattention symptoms were significantly more frequent among children aged 10-16 years with CHDs, in particular in children with corrected Tetralogy of Fallot.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Holst, Line M","Kronborg, Jonas B","Jepsen, Jens R M","Christensen, Jette Ø","Vejlstrup, Niels G","Juul, Klaus","Bjerre, Jesper Vandborg","Bilenberg, Niels","Ravn, Hanne B"],"cuid":["S03-099.92-026320"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Holst, Line M."],"keyword":["Adolescents","Attention deficit hyperactivity disorder","CHDs","Cardiac surgery","DEFICIT HYPERACTIVITY DISORDER","Heart disease","NEURODEVELOPMENTAL OUTCOMES","Prevalence","Psychiatric disorders","Psychometric properties","Quality of Life","Tetralogy of Fallot","Transposition of the Greater Arteries","Ventricular septal defect"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"attention deficit hyperactivity disorder symptoms in children with surgically corrected ventricular septal defect transposition of the great arteries and tetralogy of fallot","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/289984282/Attention_deficit_hyperactivity_disorder_symptoms_in_children_with_surgically_corrected_Ventricular_Septal_Defect_Transposition_of_the_Great_Arteries_and_Tetralogy_of_Fallot_accepted_version_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S03-099.92-026320","identifier":[{"id":"31928549","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000537649000005","type":"wos"},{"id":"85078048844","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-bbce7adc-6618-4bb5-86fd-d8e08bee1a40","ku-f472e78e-eab5-4a2d-93ef-399374bb1f47","sdu-13e3e71c-c1b1-47b8-9172-4a8cca5a6e1f"],"keyword":["ADOLESCENTS","CARDIAC-SURGERY","CHDs","DEFICIT HYPERACTIVITY DISORDER","HEART-DISEASE","NEURODEVELOPMENTAL OUTCOMES","PREVALENCE","PSYCHIATRIC-DISORDERS","PSYCHOMETRIC PROPERTIES","QUALITY-OF-LIFE","SCALE ADHD-RS","Tetralogy of Fallot","Transposition of the Greater Arteries","Ventricular Septal Defect","attention-deficit/hyperactivity disorder"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-A3FA581C3F01EB481C791B7C27FD5F5A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/171917295/Manuscript_ADHD_R2_031119.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/289984282/Attention_deficit_hyperactivity_disorder_symptoms_in_children_with_surgically_corrected_Ventricular_Septal_Defect_Transposition_of_the_Great_Arteries_and_Tetralogy_of_Fallot_accepted_version_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Paediatrics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, BRIDGE - Brain Research - Inter Disciplinary Guided Excellence (Odense)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, Research Unit of Child and Adolescent Psychiatry (Southern Denmark)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Anaesthesiology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Line M.","key":"holstpau","last":"Holst","name":"Holst, Line M.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jonas B.","key":"kronborgpau","last":"Kronborg","name":"Kronborg, Jonas B.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jens R.M.","key":"jepsenpau","last":"Jepsen","name":"Jepsen, Jens R.M.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jette","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Jette","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Niels G.","key":"vejlstruppau","last":"Vejlstrup","name":"Vejlstrup, Niels G.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Klaus","key":"juulpau","last":"Juul","name":"Juul, Klaus","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper V","key":"bjerrepau","last":"Bjerre","locid":"88b6b510-516e-4eb2-a040-91ea40ee55ae","name":"Bjerre, Jesper Vandborg","name_org":"Bjerre, Jesper V","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Niels","key":"bilenbergpau","last":"Bilenberg","locid":"c865af0f-affd-44a4-b9fa-39c26141d3e2","name":"Bilenberg, Niels","orcid":"0000-0002-5838-556X","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Hanne B.","key":"ravnpau","last":"Ravn","locid":"3049e7b7-0f18-413b-88ab-a3d77ebc079b","name":"Ravn, Hanne Berg","name_org":"Ravn, Hanne B.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31928549"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1017/s1047951119003184","issn":["10479511","14671107"],"issn_org":["10479511"],"issue":"2","journal":"Cardiology in the Young","pages":"180-187","publisher":"Cambridge University Press","status":"p","title":"Cardiology in the Young","volume":"30"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85078048844"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-bbce7adc-6618-4bb5-86fd-d8e08bee1a40","ku-f472e78e-eab5-4a2d-93ef-399374bb1f47","sdu-13e3e71c-c1b1-47b8-9172-4a8cca5a6e1f"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Attention-deficit/hyperactivity disorder symptoms in children with surgically corrected Ventricular Septal Defect, Transposition of the Great Arteries, and Tetralogy of Fallot","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-099.92-026320","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Terrorists use violence in pursuit of political goals. While terror often has severe consequences for victims, it remains an open question how terror attacks affect the general population. We study the behavioral response of citizens of cities affected by $7$ different terror attacks. We compare real-time mobile communication patterns in the first $24$ hours following a terror attack to the corresponding patterns on days with no terror attack. On ordinary days, the group of female and male participants have different activity patterns. Following a terror attack, however, we observe a significant increase of the gender differences. Knowledge about citizens' behavior response patterns following terror attacks may have important implications for the public response during and after an attack.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Juul, Jonas S.","Alessandretti, Laura","Dammeyer, Jesper","Zettler, Ingo","Lehmann, Sune","Mathiesen, Joachim"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-765099"],"filters":{"added":"2024-11","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["cs SI","physics soc ph"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"gender specific behavior change following terror attacks","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dw","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/405876387/2004.02957v1.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-765099","ids":["ku-7577ea33-a795-4dc1-ab52-4bbf2c733d38"],"keyword":["cs.SI","physics.soc-ph"],"lang":"Undetermined","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-B7A1A1D57A4ED1B21E07D8155B4DDBF9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/405876387/2004.02957v1.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Niels Bohr Institute, Biocomplexity"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jonas S.","key":"juulpau","last":"Juul","locid":"4298e83e-ac49-4e04-9ea8-f26559478f2b","name":"Juul, Jonas S.","orcid":"0000-0002-5728-9269","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Laura","key":"alessandrettipau","last":"Alessandretti","locid":"3f3d0ac1-d127-4134-81f8-739cbc2ad7c4","name":"Alessandretti, Laura","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"dammeyerpau","last":"Dammeyer","locid":"4e00d381-dd0b-4b42-a335-652388c7f73b","name":"Dammeyer, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0001-6753-8516","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ingo","key":"zettlerpau","last":"Zettler","locid":"97f75ec6-e574-4f43-8b3a-6a57c6515cab","name":"Zettler, Ingo","orcid":"0000-0001-6140-7160","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sune","key":"lehmannpau","last":"Lehmann","locid":"a5480168-96ea-448f-bb1f-5382a8436068","name":"Lehmann, Sune","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Joachim","key":"mathiesenpau","last":"Mathiesen","locid":"cd2606a2-f61e-4bf0-bcfb-b4888682b5ad","name":"Mathiesen, Joachim","orcid":"0000-0002-5621-5487","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-7577ea33-a795-4dc1-ab52-4bbf2c733d38"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Gender-specific behavior change following terror attacks","type":"Working Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-765099","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Serial assessments of measurable (or minimal) residual disease (MRD) by qPCR may identify nascent relapse in children with acute myeloid leukaemia (AML) and enable pre-emptive therapy. We investigated the kinetics and prognostic impact of recurrent fusion transcripts (RUNX1-RUNX1T1, CBFB-MYH11, KMT2A-MLLT3 or KMT2A-ELL) in 774 post-induction samples from bone marrow (BM, 347) and peripheral blood (PB, 427) from 75 children with AML. BM MRD persistence during consolidation did not increase the risk of relapse, and MRD at therapy completion did not correlate to outcome (HR = 0·64/MRD log reduction (CI: 0·32-1·26), P = 0·19). In contrast, 8/8 patients with detectable MRD in PB after first consolidation relapsed. Persistence (n = 4) and shifting from negative to positive (n = 10) in PB during follow-up predicted relapse in 14/14 patients. All 253 PB samples collected during follow-up from 36 patients in continuous complete remission were MRD negative. In core-binding factor AML, persistent low-level MRD positivity in BM during follow-up was frequent but an increment to above 5 × 10-4 heralded subsequent haematological relapse in 12/12 patients. We demonstrate that MRD monitoring in PB after induction therapy is highly informative and propose an MRD increment above 5 × 10-4 in PB and BM as a definition of molecular relapse since it always leads to haematological relapse.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Juul-Dam, Kristian Løvvik","Ommen, Hans Beier","Nyvold, Charlotte Guldborg","Walter, Christiane","Vålerhaugen, Helen","Kairisto, Veli","Abrahamsson, Jonas","Alm, Sofie J","Jahnukainen, Kirsi","Lausen, Birgitte","Reinhardt, Dirk","Zeller, Bernward","von Neuhoff, Nils","Fogelstrand, Linda","Hasle, Henrik"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-016347"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Juul-Dam, Kristian Løvvik"],"country":["Finland","Germany","Norway","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Children's Hospital Helsinki","Essen University Hospital","Oslo University Hospital","Sahlgrenska University Hospital","Turku University Hospital","University of Duisburg-Essen","University of Gothenburg","University of Helsinki","University of Oslo","University of Turku"],"keyword":["Acute myeloid leukaemia","Measurable residual disease","Relapse","fusion transcripts","paediatric haematology"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"measurable residual disease assessment by qpcr in peripheral blood is an informative tool for disease surveillance in childhood acute myeloid leukaemia","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/170281022/bjh.16560.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-016347","identifier":[{"id":"85081714954","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32175599","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-33183195-e00f-41ef-b4a1-c3185107ba0e","sdu-8b5915d8-0bd5-4beb-a12b-34fcebdf29e4"],"keyword":["acute myeloid leukaemia","fusion transcripts","measurable residual disease","paediatric haematology","relapse"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-CBA4A2D64A488747E8C5B80B29E58D20"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/170281022/bjh.16560.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aa