{"abstract":"Manipulation af data er et undervisningsforløb til matematik til grundskolens ældste klasser, som handler om at lære at forholde sig til data og forhold sig kritisk til hvordan statistik kan bruges i forskellige sammenhænge - både via manipulationer og objektive tilgange. Forløbet er en del EMU´s \"digital dømmekraft\"","author_count":1,"contributors":["Hansen, Jonas Juul"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-689230"],"filters":{"added":"2023-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Børn og unge","Dannelse","Digital dannelse","Dømmekraft","Læring pædagogik og undervisning","Matematik","Skoler fag og institutioner","Statistik","Statistikundervisning","Statistisk Analyse","Undervisning"],"level":"edu","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-UC"],"level3":{"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-KP"]},"level3all":["DI-UC-KP"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"manipulation af data","src":["kp"],"src-code":["DI-UC-KP"],"type":"doo","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-689230","ids":["kp-e666c502-9d2d-4d7c-804a-f5feebec8fdd"],"keyword":["Børn og unge","Dannelse","Digital dannelse","Dømmekraft","Læring, pædagogik og undervisning","Matematik","Skoler, fag og institutioner","Statistikundervisning","Undervisning","statistik","statistisk analyse"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Educational","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-C0B4CA614CB391781EEEB151AC51A80F"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"kp university college copenhagen","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-KP","l3nl":"KP","l3nn":"KP University College Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KP University College Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Professionshøjskole, Rektors område, Fakultet for læreruddannelse og livslang læring - Dekan, CFU Vejledning og formidling"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-KP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas Juul","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"869fff1a-19d9-4da5-86c2-ca41f1ce3968","name":"Hansen, Jonas Juul","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"publisher":"Undervisningsministeriet","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","KP","University Colleges"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["kp-e666c502-9d2d-4d7c-804a-f5feebec8fdd"],"src":["KP University College Copenhagen"],"title":"Manipulation af data","type":"Other-Unknown","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-689230","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: Augmenting nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide (NAD+) metabolism through dietary provision of NAD+ precursor vitamins translates to improved glucose handling in rodent models of obesity and diabetes. Preclinical evidence suggests that the NAD+/SIRT1 axis may be implicated in modulating important gut-related aspects of glucose regulation. We sought to test whether NAD+ precursor supplementation with nicotinamide riboside (NR) affects β-cell function, α-cell function, and incretin hormone secretion as well as circulating bile acid levels in humans. DESIGN: A 12-week randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled, parallel-group trial in 40 males with obesity and insulin resistance allocated to NR at 1000 mg twice daily (n = 20) or placebo (n = 20). Two-hour 75-g oral glucose tolerance tests were performed before and after the intervention, and plasma concentrations of glucose, insulin, C-peptide, glucagon, glucagon-like peptide 1 (GLP-1), and glucose-dependent insulinotropic polypeptide (GIP) were determined. β-Cell function indices were calculated based on glucose, insulin, and C-peptide measurements. Fasting plasma concentrations of bile acids were determined. RESULTS: NR supplementation during 12 weeks did not affect fasting or postglucose challenge concentrations of glucose, insulin, C-peptide, glucagon, GLP-1, or GIP, and β-cell function did not respond to the intervention. Additionally, no changes in circulating adipsin or bile acids were observed following NR supplementation. CONCLUSION: The current study does not provide evidence to support that dietary supplementation with the NAD+ precursor NR serves to impact glucose tolerance, β-cell secretory capacity, α-cell function, and incretin hormone secretion in nondiabetic males with obesity. Moreover, bile acid levels in plasma did not change in response to NR supplementation.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Dollerup, Ole L","Trammell, Samuel A J","Hartmann, Bolette","Holst, Jens Juul","Christensen, Britt","Møller, Niels","Gillum, Matthew P","Treebak, Jonas T","Jessen, Niels"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-025706"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Beta cell function","Fatty liver disease","Glucagon","Impaired glucose tolerance","Insulin secretion","Metabolism","ORAL GLUCOSE","Resistance","SIRT1"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effects of nicotinamide riboside on endocrine pancreatic function and incretin hormones in nondiabetic men with obesity","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85073183847&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-025706","identifier":[{"id":"31390002","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000497979600085","type":"wos"},{"id":"85073183847","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-b2f7e12c-8a00-4d52-8efd-841666391c01","ku-a7c167bb-2ea8-4bba-a401-f0740f3c5c1e"],"keyword":["BETA-CELL FUNCTION","FATTY LIVER-DISEASE","GLUCAGON","IMPAIRED GLUCOSE-TOLERANCE","INSULIN-SECRETION","METABOLISM","MONONUCLEOTIDE","ORAL GLUCOSE","RESISTANCE","SIRT1"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-F40983F6A2703AB0B911C8C8CC2E4569"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Biomedicine, Department of Biomedicine - Research and Education, Bartholin Building","Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Medical Research Laboratory"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ole L","key":"dolleruppau","last":"Dollerup","locid":"571b3fca-42a9-44aa-853b-054665af5b80","name":"Dollerup, Ole L","orcid":"0000-0001-6924-7114","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Samuel A.J.","key":"trammellpau","last":"Trammell","locid":"051c3035-15c4-456f-a77e-8ce20970d70c","name":"Trammell, Samuel A.J.","orcid":"0000-0002-5941-4094","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Bolette","key":"hartmannpau","last":"Hartmann","locid":"eb04fc6b-068a-4d5b-a106-1b7be3f7e12b","name":"Hartmann, Bolette","orcid":"0000-0001-8509-2036","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jens J.","key":"holstpau","last":"Holst","locid":"864b6401-9024-4773-9bdb-f4d4ca57dcad","name":"Holst, Jens Juul","name_org":"Holst, Jens J.","orcid":"0000-0001-6853-3805","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Britt","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"818501d4-b691-497c-b25b-b792b1040bc0","name":"Christensen, Britt","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Niels","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"2e0d8e2a-2da1-4d55-b2da-0a25c0375b1e","name":"Møller, Niels","orcid":"0000-0001-5627-7322","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Matthew P.","key":"gillumpau","last":"Gillum","locid":"65c5e8eb-5634-45db-952e-d28bf525bd32","name":"Gillum, Matthew P.","orcid":"0000-0003-4893-012X","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jonas T.","key":"treebakpau","last":"Treebak","locid":"a648ef82-ccb3-4add-83c1-384e0d90952b","name":"Treebak, Jonas T.","orcid":"0000-0003-1488-7012","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Niels","key":"jessenpau","last":"Jessen","locid":"f0d20e5e-d5b5-44da-980e-3e052af18b46","name":"Jessen, Niels","orcid":"0000-0001-5613-7274","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31390002"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1210/jc.2019-01081","issn":["0021972X","19457197"],"issn_org":["0021972X"],"issue":"11","journal":"Journal of Clinical Endocrinology and Metabolism","pages":"5703-5714","status":"p","title":"Journal of Clinical Endocrinology and Metabolism","title_org":"The Journal of clinical endocrinology and metabolism","volume":"104"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85073183847"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-b2f7e12c-8a00-4d52-8efd-841666391c01","ku-a7c167bb-2ea8-4bba-a401-f0740f3c5c1e"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Effects of Nicotinamide Riboside on Endocrine Pancreatic Function and Incretin Hormones in Nondiabetic Men With Obesity","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-025706","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Objective: To describe the impact of CHD surgery in early childhood on quality of life in children aged 10-16 years with surgically corrected Ventricular Septal Defect, Transposition of the Great Arteries, and Tetralogy of Fallot.Method: A cross-sectional survey study of quality of life survey on 161 children and adolescents aged 10-16 years with surgically corrected Ventricular Septal Defect, Transposition of the Great Arteries, and Tetralogy of Fallot. The international Paediatric Quality of Life 4.0 quality of life questionnaires were applied and collected for assessment from patients and parents. The endpoints were total, physical, emotional, social, and school quality of life scores.Results: The quality of life total and school scores was significantly lower in children with CHD than their healthy peers. There was no significant difference in quality of life between the three CHD groups. All three CHD groups had a significantly lower total (7.7-13.2%, p<0.001) and school scores (21.1-31.6%, p<0.001) than the control group. The tetralogy of Fallot group was the only group that had significantly lower scores in the physical subscale (p<0.001) than the controls.Conclusion: Children and adolescents with surgically corrected CHD show losses in quality of life in total and school scores compared to healthy controls. The tetralogy of Fallot group was the only CHD group that had significantly lower physical score than the controls.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Holst, Line M.","Kronborg, Jonas B.","Idorn, Lars","Bjerre, Jesper Vandborg","Vejlstrup, Niels","Juul, Klaus","Ravn, Hanne B."],"cuid":["S02-100.00-027360"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Holst, Line M."],"keyword":["CHD","Quality of Life","Questionnaire","Tetralogy of Fallot","Transposition of the Great Arteries","Ventricular septal defect"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"impact of congenital heart surgery on quality of life in children and adolescents with surgically corrected ventricular septal defect tetralogy of fallot and transposition of the great arteries","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85068763888&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-027360","identifier":[{"id":"31284891","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85068763888","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-cab1d18b-ede7-4bf3-b9d1-847c2cedce72","ku-f08d27a8-e681-4831-8ab7-32f33a67ee66"],"keyword":["CHD","Quality of life","Tetralogy of Fallot","Transposition of the Great Arteries","Ventricular Septal Defect","questionnaire"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-B0622ED73178F4A70098D26D8A084720"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Paediatrics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Anaesthesiology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Line M.","key":"holstpau","last":"Holst","name":"Holst, Line M.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jonas B.","key":"kronborgpau","last":"Kronborg","name":"Kronborg, Jonas B.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars","key":"idornpau","last":"Idorn","name":"Idorn, Lars","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper V.","key":"bjerrepau","last":"Bjerre","locid":"88b6b510-516e-4eb2-a040-91ea40ee55ae","name":"Bjerre, Jesper Vandborg","name_org":"Bjerre, Jesper V.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Niels","key":"vejlstruppau","last":"Vejlstrup","name":"Vejlstrup, Niels","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Klaus","key":"juulpau","last":"Juul","name":"Juul, Klaus","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","first":"Hanne B.","key":"ravnpau","last":"Ravn","locid":"3049e7b7-0f18-413b-88ab-a3d77ebc079b","name":"Ravn, Hanne Berg","name_org":"Ravn, Hanne B.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31284891"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1017/s1047951119001604","issn":["10479511","14671107"],"issn_org":["10479511"],"issue":"8","journal":"Cardiology in the Young","pages":"1082-1087","publisher":"Cambridge University Press","status":"p","title":"Cardiology in the Young","volume":"29"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85068763888"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-cab1d18b-ede7-4bf3-b9d1-847c2cedce72","ku-f08d27a8-e681-4831-8ab7-32f33a67ee66"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Impact of congenital heart surgery on quality of life in children and adolescents with surgically corrected Ventricular Septal Defect, Tetralogy of Fallot, and Transposition of the Great Arteries","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-027360","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"I artiklen anmeldes FP9 - prøven med hjælpemidler i matematik maj 2019","author_count":1,"contributors":["Hansen, Jonas Juul"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-391523"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Læring pædagogik og undervisning","Matematik","Matematikdidaktik","Matematikundervisning"],"level":"pop","oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-UC"],"level3":{"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-KP"]},"level3all":["DI-UC-KP"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"anmeldelse af fp000000000009 prøven med hjælpemidler i matematik maj 000000002019","src":["kp"],"src-code":["DI-UC-KP"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-391523","ids":["kp-c5129e25-09eb-4fc7-8cdd-cf47de970e5e"],"keyword":["Læring, pædagogik og undervisning","matematik","matematikdidaktik","matematikundervisning"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","noi":["Local-1-1-F203C4BA740E43FA6ACA87F72C2CD4C0"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"kp university college copenhagen","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-KP","l3nl":"KP","l3nn":"KP University College Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KP University College Copenhagen","namevar":["Professionshøjskolen UCC (ophørt), CFU København"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-KP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas Juul","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"869fff1a-19d9-4da5-86c2-ca41f1ce3968","name":"Hansen, Jonas Juul","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["0109937X"],"issue":"4","journal":"Matematik","pages":"8-14","publisher":"Danmarks Matematiklærerforening","status":"p","title":"Matematik","volume":"47"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","KP","University Colleges"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["kp-c5129e25-09eb-4fc7-8cdd-cf47de970e5e"],"src":["KP University College Copenhagen"],"title":"Anmeldelse af FP9 - : Prøven med hjælpemidler i matematik maj 2019","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-391523","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVES: GPR142, which is highly expressed in pancreatic islets, has recently been deorphanized as a receptor for aromatic amino acids; however, its physiological role and pharmacological potential is unclear. METHODS AND RESULTS: We find that GPR142 is expressed not only in β- but also in α-cells of the islets as well as in enteroendocrine cells, and we confirm that GPR142 is a highly selective sensor of essential aromatic amino acids, in particular Trp and oligopeptides with N-terminal Trp. GPR142 knock-out mice displayed a very limited metabolic phenotype but demonstrated that L-Trp induced secretion of pancreatic and gut hormones is mediated through GPR142 but that the receptor is not required for protein-induced hormone secretion. A synthetic GPR142 agonist stimulated insulin and glucagon as well as GIP, CCK, and GLP-1 secretion. In particular, GIP secretion was sensitive to oral administration of the GPR142 agonist an effect which in contrast to the other hormones was blocked by protein load. Oral administration of the GPR142 agonist increased [3H]-2-deoxyglucose uptake in muscle and fat depots mediated through insulin action while it lowered liver glycogen conceivably mediated through glucagon, and, consequently, it did not lower total blood glucose. Nevertheless, acute administration of the GPR142 agonist strongly improved oral glucose tolerance in both lean and obese mice as well as Zucker fatty rat. Six weeks in-feed chronic treatment with the GPR142 agonist did not affect body weight in DIO mice, but increased energy expenditure and carbohydrate utilization, lowered basal glucose, and improved insulin sensitivity. CONCLUSIONS: GPR142 functions as a sensor of aromatic amino acids, controlling GIP but also CCK and GLP-1 as well as insulin and glucagon in the pancreas. GPR142 agonists could have novel interesting potential in modifying metabolism through a balanced action of gut hormones as well as both insulin and glucagon.","author_count":20,"contributors":["Rudenko, Olga","Shang, Jin","Munk, Alexander","Ekberg, Jeppe Hvidtfeldt","Petersen, Natalia","Engelstoft, Maja S","Egerod, Kristoffer Lihme","Hjorth, Siv A.","Wu, Margaret","Feng, Yue","Zhou, Yun-Ping","Mokrosinski, Jacek","Thams, Peter","Reimann, Frank","Gribble, Fiona","Rehfeld, Jens F.","Holst, Jens Juul","Treebak, Jonas T.","Howard, Andrew D","Schwartz, Thue W."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-442437"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Cambridge"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the aromatic amino acid sensor gpr000000000142 controls metabolism through balanced regulation of pancreatic and gut hormones","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.molmet.2018.10.012","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-442437","identifier":[{"id":"PMC6323244","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"30472415","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85056805369","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-520e9174-bdbf-4616-8b5c-108e08cdd6f6"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FF63A9F740EAC9973D59607BEDF84770"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.molmet.2018.10.012","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/227692358/The_aromatic_amino_acid_sensor_GPR142_controls_metabolism_through_balanced_regulation_of_pancreatic_and_gut_hormones.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Basic Metabolic Research, Nutrient and Metabolite Sensing","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Basic Metabolic Research, Schwartz Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of cambridge","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Cambridge","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Olga","key":"rudenkopau","last":"Rudenko","locid":"197c0479-dbd6-49ff-a306-4a0ada4cfd72","name":"Rudenko, Olga","orcid":"0000-0002-1319-9712","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jin","key":"shangpau","last":"Shang","name":"Shang, Jin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Alexander","key":"munkpau","last":"Munk","locid":"ab57f2f1-4332-49ed-88b3-bfef8827401d","name":"Munk, Alexander","orcid":"0000-0002-4307-6668","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jeppe P.","key":"ekbergpau","last":"Ekberg","locid":"e4d4dbe1-39e1-489f-917d-0919f508fd50","name":"Ekberg, Jeppe Hvidtfeldt","name_org":"Ekberg, Jeppe P.","orcid":"0000-0003-0037-1891","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Natalia","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"bdad35c7-9ec8-4ebd-b002-c7cd6a39a006","name":"Petersen, Natalia","orcid":"0000-0001-9344-6041","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Maja S","key":"engelstoftpau","last":"Engelstoft","locid":"2d3a9c6f-95b0-4e76-8d25-af06ad33d25c","name":"Engelstoft, Maja S","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kristoffer L.","key":"egerodpau","last":"Egerod","locid":"9339170e-b668-47c5-84dd-50cb68db17bb","name":"Egerod, Kristoffer Lihme","name_org":"Egerod, Kristoffer L.","orcid":"0000-0003-2781-1594","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Siv A.","key":"hjorthpau","last":"Hjorth","locid":"55a4d23b-7003-4fc0-9d95-544bbb48f635","name":"Hjorth, Siv A.","orcid":"0000-0002-6470-650X","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Margaret","key":"wupau","last":"Wu","name":"Wu, Margaret","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Yue","key":"fengpau","last":"Feng","name":"Feng, Yue","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Yun-Ping","key":"zhoupau","last":"Zhou","name":"Zhou, Yun-Ping","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jacek","key":"mokrosinskipau","last":"Mokrosinski","locid":"2136c57b-d160-4aef-aeb9-8db692a1107e","name":"Mokrosinski, Jacek","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Peter","key":"thamspau","last":"Thams","locid":"3d99d0ae-f49a-4079-8c4f-b88c291d15b3","name":"Thams, Peter","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Frank","key":"reimannpau","last":"Reimann","name":"Reimann, Frank","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Fiona","key":"gribblepau","last":"Gribble","name":"Gribble, Fiona","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens F","key":"rehfeldpau","last":"Rehfeld","locid":"eaf0b29a-7fae-4c52-947e-9324996a4830","name":"Rehfeld, Jens F.","name_org":"Rehfeld, Jens F","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens J.","key":"holstpau","last":"Holst","locid":"864b6401-9024-4773-9bdb-f4d4ca57dcad","name":"Holst, Jens Juul","name_org":"Holst, Jens J.","orcid":"0000-0001-6853-3805","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jonas T.","key":"treebakpau","last":"Treebak","locid":"a648ef82-ccb3-4add-83c1-384e0d90952b","name":"Treebak, Jonas T.","orcid":"0000-0003-1488-7012","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Andrew D","key":"howardpau","last":"Howard","name":"Howard, Andrew D","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thue W","key":"schwartzpau","last":"Schwartz","locid":"c5b7c219-e499-427a-99fa-35fa233e432b","name":"Schwartz, Thue W.","name_org":"Schwartz, Thue W","orcid":"0000-0002-0261-6904","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30472415"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.molmet.2018.10.012","issn":["22128778"],"journal":"Molecular Metabolism","pages":"49-64","status":"p","title":"Molecular Metabolism","volume":"19"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85056805369"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-520e9174-bdbf-4616-8b5c-108e08cdd6f6"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The aromatic amino acid sensor GPR142 controls metabolism through balanced regulation of pancreatic and gut hormones","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-442437","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Biological, engineered and social systems often consist of many interacting parts. Sometimes the interactions between these smaller components give rise to macroscopic behavior. From stem cells joining their efforts to create a fetus capable ofliving, to social interactions allowing diseases to spread, interacting populations on many different scales exhibit dynamics that are important to study and understand. In this dissertation, numerical, analytical, and statistical methods are used to study the dynamics of systems consisting of interacting components. The thesis contains three parts. In Part I, a system of coupled oscillating stem cells in mouse embryos is studied. The stem cells create the complex spatial pattern of vertebrae precursors – somites – in mice. We develop a theoretical framework for a recently proposed mechanism for the size and timing of somite creation. We use the theory to establish previously unknown relations between key variables in the biological system, and show that the experimental values of these variables are consistent with the proposed mechanism. We also suggest experiments capable of falsifying the proposed mechanism. In another study, we show how to control experimentally observed phase waves.This method could be used as a means of testing whether these waves are critical to the timing of somites, which is a widespread hypothesis in the field. In Part II, we study the impact of contagion in networked populations. Firstly, we consider a model of complex contagion with synergy. Combining analytical and numerical analyses, we find that the synergistic effects determine which nodes can be infected and which cannot. Secondly, in another study, we examine the impact of anti-establishment nodes in a model of complex contagion describing the spread of two competing products. The model is inspired by recent anti-establishment outcomes in elections and referendums. We find that a very small number of antiestablishment nodes can cause an otherwise insignificant product to become the most adopted at equilibrium. We also argue why a few nodes can have such a considerable influence. Finally, we study what impact mutant contagion, such as the 1918 Spanish flu, has in structured populations. We analytically derive a scaling law for this impact in infinite-dimensional networks. We find that numerical analyses and existing empirical results for meme-spreading on Facebook support this law. In Part III of this dissertation, telecommunication in human populations is studied. In one paper, we examine correlations between narcissistic personality traits and social behaviour. We find correlations between the number of social contacts nodes have and their narcissistic scores. We also find evidence of homophily in socalled narcissistic admiration. The observations are in agreement with some existing hypotheses regarding the psychology of grandiose narcissists. In the final paper, we examine telecommunication patterns following terror attacks in several Western European cities. We find that, although both females and males change behaviour following terror attacks, there are significant gender differences between the changes of behaviour.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Juul, Jonas S."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-510545"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"synchronisation shocks and contagion in a connected world","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"do","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-510545","ids":["ku-c42e13db-443f-4537-828c-93a1f2a042d8"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-B4183C655080645AE40246464F8E5BE6"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copen