{"abstract":"Severe knee injuries can occur due to biomechanical factors such as knee joint laxity. Generalised Joint Hypermobility (GJH) has been proposed as an intrinsic risk factor for knee injuries in adults and adolescents, as individuals with GJH often have knee joint hypermobility. Also, critical knee injuries are known to be associated with an increased risk for future development of osteoarthritis (OA).","author_count":5,"contributors":["Junge, Tina","Juul-Kristensen, Birgit","Bloch Thorlund, Jonas","Søgaard, Karen","Wedderkopp, Niels"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-649615"],"event":{"end":"2015-01-01","place":"Odense, dk","start":"2015-01-01","title":"THE 6TH ANNUAL MEETING OF THE DANISH BIOMECHANICAL SOCIETY","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-UCL"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"neuromuscular knee joint control in adolescents with and without generalised joint hypermobility during landing in the single leg hop for distance test","src":["ucl"],"src-code":["DI-UC-UCL"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-649615","ids":["ucl-e02da586-7ee4-4f0b-99a7-3da297bd587c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","noi":["Local-1-1-FFBFC539236BEFEF89C7C198CD390428"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ucl university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-UCL","l3nl":"UCL University College","l3nn":"UCL University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"UCL University College","namevar":["UCL Erhvervsakademi og Professionshøjskole, Direktion, Sundhed, Anvendt Sundhedsforskning","UCL Erhvervsakademi og Professionshøjskole, Direktion, Sundhed, Fysioterapeutuddannelsen"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-UCL","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["University of Southern Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tina","key":"jungepau","last":"Junge","locid":"248f2025-f601-4572-adb6-13dc9a92b598","name":"Junge, Tina","orcid":"0000-0002-3304-3010","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Birgit","key":"juulkristensenpau","last":"Juul-Kristensen","name":"Juul-Kristensen, Birgit","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas","key":"blochthorlundpau","last":"Bloch Thorlund","name":"Bloch Thorlund, Jonas","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Karen","key":"søgaardpau","last":"Søgaard","name":"Søgaard, Karen","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels","key":"wedderkopppau","last":"Wedderkopp","name":"Wedderkopp, Niels","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","UCL University College","Universities","University Colleges","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ucl-e02da586-7ee4-4f0b-99a7-3da297bd587c"],"src":["UCL University College"],"title":"Neuromuscular knee joint control in adolescents with and without Generalised Joint Hypermobility during landing in the Single leg Hop for Distance test.","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-649615","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Generalised Joint Hypermobility (GJH) is considered an intrinsic risk factor for knee injuries. Knee neuromuscular control during landing may be altered in GJH due to reduced passive stability. The aim was to identify differences in knee neuromuscular control during landing of the Single-Leg-Hop-for-Distance test (SLHD) in 25 children with GJH compared to 29 children without GJH (controls), all 10-15 years. Inclusion criteria for GJH: Beighton score ≥5/9 and minimum one hypermobile knee. EMG was recorded from the quadriceps, the hamstring and the calf muscles, presented relative to Maximum Voluntary Electrical activity (MVE). There was no difference in jump length between groups. Before landing, GJH had 33% lower Semitendinosus, but 32% higher Gastrocnemius Medialis activity and 39% higher co-contraction of the lateral knee muscles, than controls. After landing, GJH had 36% lower Semitendinosus activity than controls, all significant findings. Although the groups performed equally in SLHD, GJH had a Gastrocnemius Medialis-dominated neuromuscular strategy before landing, plausibly caused by reduced Semitendinosus activity. Reduced Semitendinosus activity was seen in GJH after landing, but with no compensatory Gastrocnemius Medialis activity. Reduced pre and post-activation of the Semitendinosus may present a risk factor for traumatic knee injuries as ACL ruptures in GJH with knee hypermobility","author_count":5,"contributors":["Junge, Tina","Juul-Kristensen, B","Bloch Thorlund, Jonas","Søgaard, K","Wedderkopp, N"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-647502"],"event":{"end":"2015-01-01","place":"dk","start":"2015-01-01","title":"Conference for Danish Physiotherapists. First price for best poster","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-UCL"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"altered knee joint neuromuscular control during landing from a jump in 000000000010 000000000015 year old children with generalised joint hypermobility a substudy of the champs study denmark","src":["ucl"],"src-code":["DI-UC-UCL"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-647502","ids":["ucl-47cb3266-dbda-4646-9f7f-76ee244ef322"],"lang":"English","level":"Popular","noi":["Local-1-1-0DCFCC8E47CB6BFAF0BEA361C561EE5E"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ucl university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-UCL","l3nl":"UCL University College","l3nn":"UCL University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"UCL University College","namevar":["UCL Erhvervsakademi og Professionshøjskole, Direktion, Sundhed, Anvendt Sundhedsforskning","UCL Erhvervsakademi og Professionshøjskole, Direktion, Sundhed, Fysioterapeutuddannelsen"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-UCL","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["University of Southern Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tina","key":"jungepau","last":"Junge","locid":"248f2025-f601-4572-adb6-13dc9a92b598","name":"Junge, Tina","orcid":"0000-0002-3304-3010","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"B","key":"juulkristensenpau","last":"Juul-Kristensen","name":"Juul-Kristensen, B","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas","key":"blochthorlundpau","last":"Bloch Thorlund","name":"Bloch Thorlund, Jonas","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"K","key":"søgaardpau","last":"Søgaard","name":"Søgaard, K","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"N","key":"wedderkopppau","last":"Wedderkopp","name":"Wedderkopp, N","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","UCL University College","Universities","University Colleges","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ucl-47cb3266-dbda-4646-9f7f-76ee244ef322"],"src":["UCL University College"],"title":"Altered knee joint neuromuscular control during landing from a jump in 10-15 year old children with generalised joint hypermobility. A substudy of the CHAMPS-study Denmark.","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-647502","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Generalised Joint Hypermobility (GJH) is considered an intrinsic risk factor for knee injuries. Knee neuromuscular control during landing may be altered in GJH due to reduced passive stability. The aim was to identify differences in knee neuromuscular control during landing of the Single-Leg-Hop-for-Distance test (SLHD) in 25 children with GJH compared to 29 children without GJH (controls), all 10-15years. Inclusion criteria for GJH: Beighton score⩾5/9 and minimum one hypermobile knee. EMG was recorded from the quadriceps, the hamstring and the calf muscles, presented relative to Maximum Voluntary Electrical activity (MVE). There was no difference in jump length between groups. Before landing, GJH had 33% lower Semitendinosus, but 32% higher Gastrocnemius Medialis activity and 39% higher co contraction of the lateral knee muscles, than controls. After landing, GJH had 36% lower Semitendinosus activity than controls, all significant findings. Although the groups performed equally in SLHD, GJH had a Gastrocnemius Medialis dominated neuromuscular strategy before landing, plausibly caused by reduced Semitendinosus activity. Reduced Semitendinosus activity was seen in GJH after landing, but with no compensatory Gastrocnemius Medialis activity. Reduced pre and post-activation of the Semitendinosus may present a risk factor for traumatic knee injuries as ACL ruptures in GJH with knee hypermobility.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Junge, Tina","Wedderkopp, Niels","Thorlund, Jonas Bloch","Søgaard, Karen","Juul-Kristensen, Birgit"],"cuid":["S02-097.72-049281"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Physiotherapy"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-UCL"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"altered knee joint neuromuscular control during landing from a jump in 000000000010 000000000015year old children with generalised joint hypermobility a substudy of the champs study denmark","src":["sdu","ucl"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-UCL"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jelekin.2015.02.011","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-097.72-049281","identifier":[{"id":"25801907","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84929048178","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-9ab48256-d09d-401a-9568-fb7ede5b7ef8","ucl-81bd8fde-5197-41a2-8fbd-2b9de28adf69"],"keyword":["physiotherapy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-07D77A707062005E48B227BE2D91C85B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://ucviden.ucl.dk/ws/files/30361886/Junge._Altered_knee_joint_neuromuscular_control.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/128957561/Altered_knee_joint_neuromuscular_control_during_landing_from_a_jump_in_10_15year_old_children_with_Generalised_Joint_Hypermobility._A_substudy_of_the_CHAMPS_study_Denmark.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jelekin.2015.02.011","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Lillebælt Hospital","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, Spine Center of Southern Denmark","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, D