{"abstract":"Severe knee injuries can occur due to biomechanical factors such as knee joint laxity. Generalised Joint Hypermobility (GJH) has been proposed as an intrinsic risk factor for knee injuries in adults and adolescents, as individuals with GJH often have knee joint hypermobility. Also, critical knee injuries are known to be associated with an increased risk for future development of osteoarthritis (OA).","author_count":5,"contributors":["Junge, Tina","Juul-Kristensen, B","Thorlund, Jonas Bloch","Søgaard, K","Wedderkopp, Niels"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-649705"],"event":{"end":"2014-01-01","place":"Paris, fr","start":"2014-01-01","title":"Osteoarthritis Research Society International World Conference","year":"2014"},"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-UCL"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"neuromuscular knee joint control in adolescents with and without generalised joint hypermobility during landing in the single leg hop for distance test","src":["ucl"],"src-code":["DI-UC-UCL"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-649705","ids":["ucl-e854812d-9bd2-432e-a268-5c87922b57d9"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","noi":["Local-1-1-259BC6420E76617277ACAA395648F060"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ucl university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-UCL","l3nl":"UCL University College","l3nn":"UCL University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"UCL University College","namevar":["UCL Erhvervsakademi og Professionshøjskole, Direktion, Sundhed, Anvendt Sundhedsforskning","UCL Erhvervsakademi og Professionshøjskole, Direktion, Sundhed, Fysioterapeutuddannelsen"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-UCL","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk"